{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01L3QjvhH5ydkF7o1cWRW1Sk", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t\"\"\"The metered tensor engine.\n2\t\n3\tEvery engine call advances one global odometer by a price that is a function of tensor shapes only, never of the\n4\tmachine or the values, so the same program reaches the same reading everywhere.\n5\t\n6\tThe unit is a tick, priced to be about one nanosecond of one laptop core. tools/calibrate.py measures nanoseconds per\n7\ttick for every op on real machines and fails if any op drifts more than a factor of 5 from the median, so an entry\n8\tcannot get cheap work by picking mispriced ops.\n9\t\n10\tPrices (v3), per call:\n11\t  * every call: 2000 ticks, the Python overhead of the call itself. Backward passes pay it again per node.\n12\t  * matmul of (..., m, k) @ (..., k, n): max(m, 8) * max(k, 64) * max(n, 8) / 128 plus 256, per batch element (a 2-D right side is one\n13\t    flat call, so m counts the batch and the 256 is paid once). The same again per input needing a gradient, with the\n14\t    inner and outer dimensions swapped to match the product backward actually does.\n15\t  * cheap elementwise work (add, mul, negate, compare, copy, sum): 1 tick per 4 elements. ones and full 1 per 8, and\n16\t    zeros and the backward of a sum 1 per 16 and 1 per 8, because they only fill memory.\n17\t  * sqrt, div, tanh: 1 tick per 2 elements. exp, log, sigmoid, sin, cos: 1 per element. where, power, sign: 2 per\n18\t    element. Integer % and //: 1 per element.\n19\t  * randn 4 and rand 2 per element. Logit ops (softmax, log_softmax, cross_entropy): 2 per logit, 1 per logit backward;\n20\t    cross_entropy pays the call price twice.\n21\t  * embedding: 1 per 4 elements, plus per row 8 and 2 per million table floats; backward 16 per element plus the zeroed\n22\t    table.\n23\t  * concat: 256 per input tensor on top of the elements, 1024 per input tensor backward. split: 2000 per part forward,\n24\t    512 per part backward. data.batch: 2000 plus 64 per row plus 1 per byte.\n25\t  * views (transpose, slicing, a reshape that keeps the memory) are free apart from the call price. A reshape that has\n26\t    to copy pays 1 per element.\n27\t\n28\tWhen a charge would pass the budget, the op raises BudgetExhausted and every later op raises too.\n29\t\"\"\"\n30\t\n31\timport contextlib as _contextlib\n32\timport math as _math\n33\t\n34\timport numpy as _np\n35\t\n36\t_F = _np.float32\n37\t_I = _np.int32\n38\t\n39\t\n40\tclass BudgetExhausted(Exception):\n41\t    pass\n42\t\n43\t\n44\tclass RuleViolation(Exception):\n45\t    pass\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tclass _Meter:\n49\t    def __init__(self):\n50\t        self.reset(None, 0)\n51\t\n52\t    def reset(self, budget, seed, mode=\"train\", item_cap=20_000):\n53\t        self.budget = budget\n54\t        self.used = 0\n55\t        self.exhausted = False\n56\t        self.mode = mode\n57\t        self.grad = mode == \"train\"\n58\t        self.items = 0\n59\t        self.item_cap = item_cap\n60\t        self.init_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 0])\n61\t        self.data_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 1])\n62\t\n63\t\n64\t_M = _Meter()\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t_CALL = 2000  # ticks for one engine call, whatever its size\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef _tick(n=0):\n71\t    if _M.exhausted:\n72\t        raise BudgetExhausted(\"the odometer already reached its budget\")\n73\t    n = int(n) if n > 0 else 0  # a negative price would run the odometer backwards\n74\t    n += _CALL\n75\t    if _M.budget is not None and _M.used + n > _M.budget:\n76\t        _M.exhausted = True\n77\t        raise BudgetExhausted(f\"budget {_M.budget:.3e} reached at {_M.used:.3e}\")\n78\t    _M.used += n\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef _train_only(what):\n82\t    if _M.mode != \"train\":\n83\t        raise RuleViolation(f\"{what} is not allowed during evaluation\")\n84\t\n85\t\n86\tdef used():\n87\t    return _M.used\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef budget():\n91\t    return _M.budget\n92\t\n93\t\n94\tdef remaining():\n95\t    return None if _M.budget is None else _M.budget - _M.used\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t@_contextlib.contextmanager\n99\tdef no_grad():\n100\t    prev = _M.grad\n101\t    _M.grad = False\n102\t    try:\n103\t        yield\n104\t    finally:\n105\t        _M.grad = prev\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tclass Tensor:\n109\t    \"\"\"An opaque array. Values leave the engine only through item(), which is rationed.\"\"\"\n110\t\n111\t    __slots__ = (\"_d\", \"_prev\", \"_back\", \"_rg\", \"grad\")\n112\t\n113\t    def __init__(self, d, prev=(), back=None, rg=False):\n114\t        self._d = d\n115\t        self._prev = prev\n116\t        self._back = back\n117\t        self._rg = rg\n118\t        self.grad = None\n119\t\n120\t    # ---- what an entry may know about a tensor\n121\t    @property\n122\t    def shape(self):\n123\t        return self._d.shape\n124\t\n125\t    @property\n126\t    def ndim(self):\n127\t        return self._d.ndim\n128\t\n129\t    @property\n130\t    def size(self):\n131\t        return int(self._d.size)\n132\t\n133\t    @property\n134\t    def is_int(self):\n135\t        return self._d.dtype.kind == \"i\"\n136\t\n137\t    @property\n138\t    def requires_grad(self):\n139\t        return self._rg\n140\t\n141\t    def __len__(self):\n142\t        return self._d.shape[0]\n143\t\n144\t    def __repr__(self):\n145\t        kind = \"int\" if self.is_int else \"float\"\n146\t        return f\"Tensor(shape={self.shape}, {kind})\"\n147\t\n148\t    __str__ = __repr__\n149\t\n150\t    def __format__(self, spec):\n151\t        return repr(self)\n152\t\n153\t    def __bool__(self):\n154\t        raise RuleViolation(\"a tensor has no truth value; use item()\")\n155\t\n156\t    def __float__(self):\n157\t        raise RuleViolation(\"use item() to read a scalar\")\n158\t\n159\t    __int__ = __index__ = __float__\n160\t\n161\t    def __iter__(self):\n162\t        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors are not iterable\")\n163\t\n164\t    def __array__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n165\t        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors cannot be converted to arrays\")\n166\t\n167\t    __hash__ = object.__hash__\n168\t\n169\t    def item(self):\n170\t        _train_only(\"item()\")\n171\t        if self._d.size != 1:\n172\t            raise RuleViolation(\"item() needs a one-element tensor\")\n173\t        _M.items += 1\n174\t        if _M.items > _M.item_cap:\n175\t            raise RuleViolation(f\"more than {_M.item_cap} item() reads\")\n176\t        _tick()\n177\t        return self._d.item()\n178\t\n179\t    def detach(self):\n180\t        return Tensor(self._d)\n181\t\n182\t    # ---- in-place update of a parameter (optimizers)\n183\t    def update(self, value):\n184\t        _train_only(\"update()\")\n185\t        value = _as_tensor(value, self)\n186\t        if value.shape != self.shape:\n187\t            value = Tensor(_np.broadcast_to(value._d, self.shape))\n188\t        _tick(self.size // 4)\n189\t        self._d[...] = value._d\n190\t\n191\t    # ---- autodiff\n192\t    def backward(self):\n193\t        _train_only(\"backward()\")\n194\t        if self.size != 1:\n195\t            raise RuleViolation(\"backward() needs a scalar loss\")\n196\t        order, seen, stack = [], set(), [(self, False)]\n197\t        while stack:\n198\t            node, done = stack.pop()\n199\t            if done:\n200\t                order.append(node)\n201\t                continue\n202\t            if id(node) in seen or not node._rg:\n203\t                continue\n204\t            seen.add(id(node))\n205\t            stack.append((node, True))\n206\t            for p in node._prev:\n207\t                stack.append((p, False))\n208\t        grads = {id(self): _np.ones_like(self._d)}\n209\t        for node in reversed(order):\n210\t            g = grads.pop(id(node), None)\n211\t            if g is None:\n212\t                continue\n213\t            if node._back is None:\n214\t                if node.grad is None:\n215\t                    node.grad = Tensor(g.astype(_F, copy=False))\n216\t                else:\n217\t                    _tick(g.size // 4)\n218\t                    node.grad._d = node.grad._d + g\n219\t                continue\n220\t            _tick()\n221\t            need = [p._rg for p in node._prev]\n222\t            for p, pg in zip(node._prev, node._back(g, need)):\n223\t                if pg is None or not p._rg:\n224\t                    continue\n225\t                if id(p) in grads:\n226\t                    _tick(pg.size // 4)\n227\t                    grads[id(p)] = grads[id(p)] + pg\n228\t                else:\n229\t                    grads[id(p)] = pg\n230\t            node._prev, node._back = (), None\n231\t\n232\t    # ---- operators\n233\t    def __add__(self, o):\n234\t        return add(self, o)\n235\t\n236\t    def __radd__(self, o):\n237\t        return add(o, self)\n238\t\n239\t    def __sub__(self, o):\n240\t        return sub(self, o)\n241\t\n242\t    def __rsub__(self, o):\n243\t        return sub(o, self)\n244\t\n245\t    def __mul__(self, o):\n246\t        return mul(self, o)\n247\t\n248\t    def __rmul__(self, o):\n249\t        return mul(o, self)\n250\t\n251\t    def __truediv__(self, o):\n252\t        return div(self, o)\n253\t\n254\t    def __rtruediv__(self, o):\n255\t        return div(o, self)\n256\t\n257\t    def __neg__(self):\n258\t        return neg(self)\n259\t\n260\t    def __pow__(self, p):\n261\t        return power(self, p)\n262\t\n263\t    def __matmul__(self, o):\n264\t        return matmul(self, o)\n265\t\n266\t    def __mod__(self, o):\n267\t        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.mod, per_4=4)\n268\t\n269\t    def __floordiv__(self, o):\n270\t        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.floor_divide, per_4=4)\n271\t\n272\t    def __gt__(self, o):\n273\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater)\n274\t\n275\t    def __ge__(self, o):\n276\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater_equal)\n277\t\n278\t    def __lt__(self, o):\n279\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.less)\n280\t\n281\t    def __le__(self, o):\n282\t        return _compare(self, o, _np.less_equal)\n283\t\n284\t    def __getitem__(self, key):\n285\t        return getitem(self, key)\n286\t\n287\t    def reshape(self, *shape):\n288\t        return reshape(self, *shape)\n289\t\n290\t    def transpose(self, *axes):\n291\t        return transpose(self, *axes)\n292\t\n293\t    def swapaxes(self, a, b):\n294\t        return swapaxes(self, a, b)\n295\t\n296\t    def sum(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n297\t        return sum(self, axis, keepdims)\n298\t\n299\t    def mean(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n300\t        return mean(self, axis, keepdims)\n301\t\n302\t    def max(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n303\t        return max(self, axis, keepdims)\n304\t\n305\t    def float(self):\n306\t        return to_float(self)\n307\t\n308\t    @property\n309\t    def T(self):\n310\t        return swapaxes(self, -1, -2)\n311\t\n312\t\n313\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n314\t\n315\t\n316\tdef _as_tensor(x, like=None):\n317\t    if isinstance(x, Tensor):\n318\t        return x\n319\t    if isinstance(x, bool) or not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n320\t        raise RuleViolation(f\"expected a tensor or a number, got {type(x).__name__}\")\n321\t    dtype = _I if (like is not None and like.is_int and isinstance(x, int)) else _F\n322\t    return Tensor(_np.asarray(x, dtype=dtype))\n323\t\n324\t\n325\tdef _make(d, parents, back):\n326\t    rg = _M.grad and any(p._rg for p in parents)\n327\t    return Tensor(d, parents if rg else (), back if rg else None, rg)\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tdef _unbroadcast(g, shape):\n331\t    if g.shape == shape:\n332\t        return g\n333\t    _tick(g.size // 4)\n334\t    while g.ndim > len(shape):\n335\t        g = g.sum(0)\n336\t    axes = tuple(i for i, s in enumerate(shape) if s == 1 and g.shape[i] != 1)\n337\t    return g.sum(axes, keepdims=True) if axes else g\n338\t\n339\t\n340\tdef _floats(*ts):\n341\t    for t in ts:\n342\t        if t.is_int:\n343\t            raise RuleViolation(\"this op needs float tensors; convert with .float()\")\n344\t\n345\t\n346\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- creation\n347\t\n348\t\n349\tdef param(x):\n350\t    \"\"\"Mark a tensor as a trainable leaf.\"\"\"\n351\t    _train_only(\"param()\")\n352\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n353\t    t = Tensor(_np.array(x._d, dtype=_F))\n354\t    t._rg = True\n355\t    return t\n356\t\n357\t\n358\tdef zeros(shape):\n359\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 16)\n360\t    return Tensor(_np.zeros(shape, _F))\n361\t\n362\t\n363\tdef ones(shape):\n364\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n365\t    return Tensor(_np.ones(shape, _F))\n366\t\n367\t\n368\tdef full(shape, value):\n369\t    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n370\t    return Tensor(_np.full(shape, float(value), _F))\n371\t\n372\t\n373\tdef arange(n):\n374\t    _tick(n // 4)\n375\t    return Tensor(_np.arange(n, dtype=_F))\n376\t\n377\t\n378\tdef randn(shape, std=1.0):\n379\t    _train_only(\"randn()\")\n380\t    _tick(4 * _np.prod(shape))\n381\t    return Tensor((_M.init_rng.standard_normal(shape, dtype=_F) * _F(std)).astype(_F))\n382\t\n383\t\n384\tdef rand(shape):\n385\t    _train_only(\"rand()\")\n386\t    _tick(2 * _np.prod(shape))\n387\t    return Tensor(_M.init_rng.random(shape, dtype=_F))\n388\t\n389\t\n390\tdef tril(x, k=0):\n391\t    \"\"\"Zero the elements above the k-th diagonal of the last two axes.\"\"\"\n392\t    _floats(x)\n393\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n394\t    keep = _np.tril(_np.ones(x.shape[-2:], dtype=bool), k)\n395\t    out = _np.where(keep, x._d, _F(0))\n396\t\n397\t    def back(g, need):\n398\t        _tick(2 * g.size)\n399\t        return (_np.where(keep, g, _F(0)),)\n400\t\n401\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tdef where(mask, a, b):\n405\t    \"\"\"mask is a float tensor of zeros and ones (from a comparison or tril).\"\"\"\n406\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n407\t    _floats(mask, a, b)\n408\t    m = mask._d != 0\n409\t    out = _np.where(m, a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n410\t    _tick(2 * out.size)\n411\t\n412\t    def back(g, need):\n413\t        ga = gb = None\n414\t        if need[1]:\n415\t            _tick(2 * g.size)\n416\t            ga = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, g, _F(0)), a.shape)\n417\t        if need[2]:\n418\t            _tick(2 * g.size)\n419\t            gb = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, _F(0), g), b.shape)\n420\t        return (None, ga, gb)\n421\t\n422\t    return _make(out, (mask, a, b), back)\n423\t\n424\t\n425\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elementwise\n426\t\n427\t\n428\tdef _unary(x, f, df, fwd=4, bwd=1):\n429\t    \"\"\"df(x_array, out_array, g) -> grad. fwd and bwd are prices in ticks per 4 elements.\"\"\"\n430\t    _floats(x)\n431\t    _tick(x.size * fwd // 4)\n432\t    xd = x._d\n433\t    out = f(xd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n434\t\n435\t    def back(g, need):\n436\t        _tick(g.size * bwd // 4)\n437\t        return (df(xd, out, g),)\n438\t\n439\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n440\t\n441\t\n442\tdef neg(x):\n443\t    return _unary(x, _np.negative, lambda x, y, g: -g, fwd=1)\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef exp(x):\n447\t    return _unary(x, _np.exp, lambda x, y, g: g * y)\n448\t\n449\t\n450\tdef log(x):\n451\t    return _unary(x, _np.log, lambda x, y, g: g / x, bwd=2)\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef sqrt(x):\n455\t    return _unary(x, _np.sqrt, lambda x, y, g: g * _F(0.5) / y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n456\t\n457\t\n458\tdef rsqrt(x):\n459\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / _np.sqrt(a), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(-0.5) * y * y * y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n460\t\n461\t\n462\tdef tanh(x):\n463\t    return _unary(x, _np.tanh, lambda x, y, g: g * (1 - y * y), fwd=2, bwd=4)\n464\t\n465\t\n466\tdef sigmoid(x):\n467\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / (1 + _np.exp(-a)), lambda x, y, g: g * y * (1 - y), bwd=2)\n468\t\n469\t\n470\tdef relu(x):\n471\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.maximum(a, _F(0)), lambda x, y, g: g * (x > 0), fwd=2)\n472\t\n473\t\n474\tdef sin(x):\n475\t    return _unary(x, _np.sin, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.cos(x), bwd=4)\n476\t\n477\t\n478\tdef cos(x):\n479\t    return _unary(x, _np.cos, lambda x, y, g: -g * _np.sin(x), bwd=4)\n480\t\n481\t\n482\tdef abs(x):\n483\t    return _unary(x, _np.abs, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.sign(x), fwd=1, bwd=8)\n484\t\n485\t\n486\tdef sign(x):\n487\t    \"\"\"No gradient.\"\"\"\n488\t    _floats(x)\n489\t    _tick(x.size * 2)\n490\t    return Tensor(_np.sign(x._d).astype(_F))\n491\t\n492\t\n493\tdef power(x, p):\n494\t    if not isinstance(p, (int, float)) or isinstance(p, bool):\n495\t        raise RuleViolation(\"power() takes a number exponent\")\n496\t    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.power(a, _F(p)), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(p) * _np.power(x, _F(p - 1)), fwd=8, bwd=8)\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tdef add(a, b):\n500\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n501\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n502\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.add)\n503\t    out = a._d + b._d\n504\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n505\t\n506\t    def back(g, need):\n507\t        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, _unbroadcast(g, b.shape) if need[1] else None)\n508\t\n509\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n510\t\n511\t\n512\tdef sub(a, b):\n513\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n514\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n515\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.subtract)\n516\t    out = a._d - b._d\n517\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n518\t\n519\t    def back(g, need):\n520\t        gb = None\n521\t        if need[1]:\n522\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n523\t            gb = _unbroadcast(-g, b.shape)\n524\t        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, gb)\n525\t\n526\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n527\t\n528\t\n529\tdef mul(a, b):\n530\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n531\t    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n532\t        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.multiply)\n533\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n534\t    out = ad * bd\n535\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n536\t\n537\t    def back(g, need):\n538\t        ga = gb = None\n539\t        if need[0]:\n540\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n541\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g * bd, a.shape)\n542\t        if need[1]:\n543\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n544\t            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ad, b.shape)\n545\t        return (ga, gb)\n546\t\n547\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n548\t\n549\t\n550\tdef div(a, b):\n551\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n552\t    _floats(a, b)\n553\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n554\t    out = (ad / bd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n555\t    _tick(out.size // 2)\n556\t\n557\t    def back(g, need):\n558\t        ga = gb = None\n559\t        if need[0]:\n560\t            _tick(g.size // 2)\n561\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g / bd, a.shape)\n562\t        if need[1]:\n563\t            _tick(g.size)\n564\t            gb = _unbroadcast(-g * out / bd, b.shape)\n565\t        return (ga, gb)\n566\t\n567\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n568\t\n569\t\n570\tdef maximum(a, b):\n571\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n572\t    _floats(a, b)\n573\t    out = _np.maximum(a._d, b._d)\n574\t    _tick(out.size // 2)\n575\t    pick_a = a._d >= b._d\n576\t\n577\t    def back(g, need):\n578\t        ga = gb = None\n579\t        if need[0]:\n580\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n581\t            ga = _unbroadcast(g * pick_a, a.shape)\n582\t        if need[1]:\n583\t            _tick(g.size // 4)\n584\t            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ~pick_a, b.shape)\n585\t        return (ga, gb)\n586\t\n587\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n588\t\n589\t\n590\tdef minimum(a, b):\n591\t    return neg(maximum(neg(a), neg(b)))\n592\t\n593\t\n594\tdef _compare(a, b, f):\n595\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n596\t    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n597\t    _tick(out.size // 4)\n598\t    return Tensor(out)\n599\t\n600\t\n601\tdef _int_binary(a, b, f, per_4=1):\n602\t    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n603\t    if not (a.is_int and b.is_int):\n604\t        raise RuleViolation(\"integer ops need two integer operands\")\n605\t    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_I)\n606\t    _tick(out.size * per_4 // 4)\n607\t    return Tensor(out)\n608\t\n609\t\n610\tdef to_float(x):\n611\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n612\t    return Tensor(x._d.astype(_F))\n613\t\n614\t\n615\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reductions\n616\t\n617\t\n618\tdef _norm_axis(axis, ndim):\n619\t    if axis is None:\n620\t        return tuple(range(ndim))\n621\t    axes = axis if isinstance(axis, tuple) else (axis,)\n622\t    return tuple(a % ndim for a in axes)\n623\t\n624\t\n625\tdef sum(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n626\t    _floats(x)\n627\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n628\t    out = x._d.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=keepdims, dtype=_F)\n629\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n630\t\n631\t    def back(g, need):\n632\t        _tick(x.size // 8)\n633\t        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n634\t        return (_np.broadcast_to(gk, x.shape).astype(_F),)\n635\t\n636\t    return _make(_np.asarray(out, _F), (x,), back)\n637\t\n638\t\n639\tdef mean(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n640\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n641\t    n = int(_np.prod([x.shape[a] for a in axes]))\n642\t    return mul(sum(x, axis, keepdims), 1.0 / n)\n643\t\n644\t\n645\tdef max(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n646\t    _floats(x)\n647\t    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n648\t    out = x._d.max(axis=axes, keepdims=True)\n649\t    _tick(x.size // 4)\n650\t\n651\t    def back(g, need):\n652\t        _tick(x.size)\n653\t        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n654\t        hit = x._d == out\n655\t        return (hit * gk / hit.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=True),)\n656\t\n657\t    return _make(out if keepdims else out.squeeze(axes), (x,), back)\n658\t\n659\t\n660\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shapes (views are free)\n661\t\n662\t\n663\tdef _reshaped(a, shape):\n664\t    out = a.reshape(shape)\n665\t    _tick(0 if _np.may_share_memory(out, a) else out.size)\n666\t    return out\n667\t\n668\t\n669\tdef reshape(x, *shape):\n670\t    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], tuple):\n671\t        shape = shape[0]\n672\t    src = x.shape\n673\t    return _make(_reshaped(x._d, shape), (x,), lambda g, need: (_reshaped(g, src),))\n674\t\n675\t\n676\tdef transpose(x, *axes):\n677\t    if len(axes) == 1 and isinstance(axes[0], tuple):\n678\t        axes = axes[0]\n679\t    axes = axes or tuple(reversed(range(x.ndim)))\n680\t    inv = tuple(_np.argsort(axes))\n681\t    _tick()\n682\t    return _make(x._d.transpose(axes), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.transpose(inv),))\n683\t\n684\t\n685\tdef swapaxes(x, a, b):\n686\t    _tick()\n687\t    return _make(x._d.swapaxes(a, b), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.swapaxes(a, b),))\n688\t\n689\t\n690\tdef _check_basic_key(key):\n691\t    keys = key if isinstance(key, tuple) else (key,)\n692\t    for k in keys:\n693\t        if type(k) not in (int, slice, type(None), type(...)):\n694\t            raise RuleViolation(\"indexing takes ints, slices, None and ...; use embedding() to gather\")\n695\t\n696\t\n697\tdef getitem(x, key):\n698\t    _check_basic_key(key)\n699\t    _tick()\n700\t    out = x._d[key]\n701\t    src_shape = x.shape\n702\t\n703\t    def back(g, need):\n704\t        _tick(_np.prod(src_shape) // 16 + g.size // 4)\n705\t        full_g = _np.zeros(src_shape, _F)\n706\t        full_g[key] = g\n707\t        return (full_g,)\n708\t\n709\t    if x.is_int:\n710\t        return Tensor(out)\n711\t    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n712\t\n713\t\n714\tdef split(x, sections, axis=-1):\n715\t    \"\"\"Split into equal parts (a view; the backward is a concat).\"\"\"\n716\t    parts = _np.split(x._d, sections, axis=axis)\n717\t    _tick(_CALL * len(parts))\n718\t    outs = []\n719\t    for i, part in enumerate(parts):\n720\t\n721\t        def back(g, need, i=i):\n722\t            _tick(_np.prod(x.shape) // 4 + 512 * len(parts))\n723\t            full_g = [_np.zeros_like(p) for p in parts]\n724\t            full_g[i] = g\n725\t            return (_np.concatenate(full_g, axis=axis),)\n726\t\n727\t        outs.append(_make(part, (x,), back) if not x.is_int else Tensor(part))\n728\t    return outs\n729\t\n730\t\n731\tdef concat(ts, axis=-1):\n732\t    ts = list(ts)\n733\t    out = _np.concatenate([t._d for t in ts], axis=axis)\n734\t    _tick(out.size // 4 + 256 * len(ts))\n735\t    if all(t.is_int for t in ts):\n736\t        return Tensor(out)\n737\t    _floats(*ts)\n738\t    bounds = _np.cumsum([t.shape[axis] for t in ts])[:-1]\n739\t\n740\t    def back(g, need):\n741\t        _tick(1024 * len(ts))\n742\t        return tuple(_np.split(g, bounds, axis=axis))\n743\t\n744\t    return _make(out, tuple(ts), back)\n745\t\n746\t\n747\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- matmul\n748\t\n749\t\n750\tdef _matmul_price(rows, inner, cols, calls):\n751\t    # thin products run far below BLAS's peak rate, so short sides price as if they had 8 rows or columns and 64 inner\n752\t    return calls * ((rows if rows > 8 else 8) * (cols if cols > 8 else 8) * (inner if inner > 64 else 64) // 128 + 256)\n753\t\n754\t\n755\tdef matmul(a, b):\n756\t    _floats(a, b)\n757\t    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n758\t    if ad.ndim < 2 or bd.ndim < 2:\n759\t        raise RuleViolation(\"matmul() needs tensors with at least two dimensions\")\n760\t    m, k, n = ad.shape[-2], ad.shape[-1], bd.shape[-1]\n761\t    calls = int(_np.prod(_np.broadcast_shapes(ad.shape[:-2], bd.shape[:-2])))\n762\t    if bd.ndim == 2:\n763\t        m, calls = m * calls, 1\n764\t    _tick(_matmul_price(m, k, n, calls))  # before the work, because time here is not bounded by memory\n765\t    if bd.ndim == 2 and ad.ndim > 2:\n766\t        lead = ad.shape[:-1]\n767\t        out = (ad.reshape(-1, ad.shape[-1]) @ bd).reshape(*lead, bd.shape[-1])\n768\t    else:\n769\t        out = ad @ bd\n770\t\n771\t    def back(g, need):\n772\t        ga = gb = None\n773\t        if need[0]:\n774\t            _tick(_matmul_price(m, n, k, calls))\n775\t            if bd.ndim == 2:\n776\t                ga = (g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1]) @ bd.T).reshape(ad.shape)\n777\t            else:\n778\t                ga = _unbroadcast(g @ _np.swapaxes(bd, -1, -2), ad.shape)\n779\t        if need[1]:\n780\t            _tick(_matmul_price(k, m, n, calls))\n781\t            if bd.ndim == 2:\n782\t                gb = ad.reshape(-1, k).T @ g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1])\n783\t            else:\n784\t                gb = _unbroadcast(_np.swapaxes(ad, -1, -2) @ g, bd.shape)\n785\t        return (ga, gb)\n786\t\n787\t    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n788\t\n789\t\n790\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- indexing\n791\t\n792\t\n793\tdef embedding(table, idx):\n794\t    \"\"\"Rows of a 2-D table picked by an integer tensor: out[...] = table[idx[...]].\"\"\"\n795\t    _floats(table)\n796\t    if not idx.is_int:\n797\t        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding() needs an integer index tensor\")\n798\t    ix = idx._d\n799\t    if ix.size and (ix.min() < 0 or ix.max() >= table.shape[0]):\n800\t        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding index out of range\")\n801\t    out = table._d[ix]\n802\t    _tick((8 + table.size // (1 << 19)) * ix.size + out.size // 4)  # bigger tables miss the cache on more rows\n803\t    rows = table.shape\n804\t\n805\t    def back(g, need):\n806\t        _tick(16 * g.size + table.size // 16)\n807\t        gt = _np.zeros(rows, _F)\n808\t        _np.add.at(gt, ix.reshape(-1), g.reshape(-1, rows[1]))\n809\t        return (gt, None)\n810\t\n811\t    return _make(out, (table, idx), back)\n812\t\n813\t\n814\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fused\n815\t\n816\t\n817\tdef softmax(x, axis=-1):\n818\t    _floats(x)\n819\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n820\t    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n821\t    e = _np.exp(z)\n822\t    y = e / e.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n823\t\n824\t    def back(g, need):\n825\t        _tick(x.size)\n826\t        return (y * (g - (g * y).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)),)\n827\t\n828\t    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n829\t\n830\t\n831\tdef log_softmax(x, axis=-1):\n832\t    _floats(x)\n833\t    _tick(2 * x.size)\n834\t    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n835\t    lse = _np.log(_np.exp(z).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True))\n836\t    y = z - lse\n837\t\n838\t    def back(g, need):\n839\t        _tick(x.size)\n840\t        return (g - _np.exp(y) * g.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True),)\n841\t\n842\t    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n843\t\n844\t\n845\tdef cross_entropy(logits, targets):\n846\t    \"\"\"Mean negative log-likelihood in nats. logits (..., V) float, targets (...) int.\"\"\"\n847\t    _floats(logits)\n848\t    if not targets.is_int:\n849\t        raise RuleViolation(\"cross_entropy() needs integer targets\")\n850\t    V = logits.shape[-1]\n851\t    z = logits._d.reshape(-1, V)\n852\t    t = targets._d.reshape(-1)\n853\t    _tick(2 * z.size + _CALL)\n854\t    zmax = z.max(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n855\t    e = _np.exp(z - zmax)\n856\t    s = e.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n857\t    n = z.shape[0]\n858\t    nll = (_np.log(s[:, 0]) + zmax[:, 0] - z[_np.arange(n), t]).mean()\n859\t\n860\t    def back(g, need):\n861\t        _tick(z.size)\n862\t        p = e / s\n863\t        p[_np.arange(n), t] -= 1\n864\t        return ((p * (g / n)).reshape(logits.shape).astype(_F, copy=False), None)\n865\t\n866\t    return _make(_np.asarray(nll, _F), (logits, targets), back)\n867\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c1587825-b49a-4867-a7de-efec5b369583", "uuid": "6a9b171f-0e3f-43df-a185-a64d379ef9a0", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T13:40:23.078Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/home/user/att/attempt-01/odometer/_engine.py", "content": "\"\"\"The metered tensor engine.\n\nEvery engine call advances one global odometer by a price that is a function of tensor shapes only, never of the\nmachine or the values, so the same program reaches the same reading everywhere.\n\nThe unit is a tick, priced to be about one nanosecond of one laptop core. tools/calibrate.py measures nanoseconds per\ntick for every op on real machines and fails if any op drifts more than a factor of 5 from the median, so an entry\ncannot get cheap work by picking mispriced ops.\n\nPrices (v3), per call:\n  * every call: 2000 ticks, the Python overhead of the call itself. Backward passes pay it again per node.\n  * matmul of (..., m, k) @ (..., k, n): max(m, 8) * max(k, 64) * max(n, 8) / 128 plus 256, per batch element (a 2-D right side is one\n    flat call, so m counts the batch and the 256 is paid once). The same again per input needing a gradient, with the\n    inner and outer dimensions swapped to match the product backward actually does.\n  * cheap elementwise work (add, mul, negate, compare, copy, sum): 1 tick per 4 elements. ones and full 1 per 8, and\n    zeros and the backward of a sum 1 per 16 and 1 per 8, because they only fill memory.\n  * sqrt, div, tanh: 1 tick per 2 elements. exp, log, sigmoid, sin, cos: 1 per element. where, power, sign: 2 per\n    element. Integer % and //: 1 per element.\n  * randn 4 and rand 2 per element. Logit ops (softmax, log_softmax, cross_entropy): 2 per logit, 1 per logit backward;\n    cross_entropy pays the call price twice.\n  * embedding: 1 per 4 elements, plus per row 8 and 2 per million table floats; backward 16 per element plus the zeroed\n    table.\n  * concat: 256 per input tensor on top of the elements, 1024 per input tensor backward. split: 2000 per part forward,\n    512 per part backward. data.batch: 2000 plus 64 per row plus 1 per byte.\n  * views (transpose, slicing, a reshape that keeps the memory) are free apart from the call price. A reshape that has\n    to copy pays 1 per element.\n\nWhen a charge would pass the budget, the op raises BudgetExhausted and every later op raises too.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport contextlib as _contextlib\nimport math as _math\n\nimport numpy as _np\n\n_F = _np.float32\n_I = _np.int32\n\n\nclass BudgetExhausted(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass RuleViolation(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\nclass _Meter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.reset(None, 0)\n\n    def reset(self, budget, seed, mode=\"train\", item_cap=20_000):\n        self.budget = budget\n        self.used = 0\n        self.exhausted = False\n        self.mode = mode\n        self.grad = mode == \"train\"\n        self.items = 0\n        self.item_cap = item_cap\n        self.init_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 0])\n        self.data_rng = _np.random.default_rng([seed, 1])\n\n\n_M = _Meter()\n\n\n_CALL = 2000  # ticks for one engine call, whatever its size\n\n\ndef _tick(n=0):\n    if _M.exhausted:\n        raise BudgetExhausted(\"the odometer already reached its budget\")\n    n = int(n) if n > 0 else 0  # a negative price would run the odometer backwards\n    n += _CALL\n    if _M.budget is not None and _M.used + n > _M.budget:\n        _M.exhausted = True\n        raise BudgetExhausted(f\"budget {_M.budget:.3e} reached at {_M.used:.3e}\")\n    _M.used += n\n\n\ndef _train_only(what):\n    if _M.mode != \"train\":\n        raise RuleViolation(f\"{what} is not allowed during evaluation\")\n\n\ndef used():\n    return _M.used\n\n\ndef budget():\n    return _M.budget\n\n\ndef remaining():\n    return None if _M.budget is None else _M.budget - _M.used\n\n\n@_contextlib.contextmanager\ndef no_grad():\n    prev = _M.grad\n    _M.grad = False\n    try:\n        yield\n    finally:\n        _M.grad = prev\n\n\nclass Tensor:\n    \"\"\"An opaque array. Values leave the engine only through item(), which is rationed.\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"_d\", \"_prev\", \"_back\", \"_rg\", \"grad\")\n\n    def __init__(self, d, prev=(), back=None, rg=False):\n        self._d = d\n        self._prev = prev\n        self._back = back\n        self._rg = rg\n        self.grad = None\n\n    # ---- what an entry may know about a tensor\n    @property\n    def shape(self):\n        return self._d.shape\n\n    @property\n    def ndim(self):\n        return self._d.ndim\n\n    @property\n    def size(self):\n        return int(self._d.size)\n\n    @property\n    def is_int(self):\n        return self._d.dtype.kind == \"i\"\n\n    @property\n    def requires_grad(self):\n        return self._rg\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return self._d.shape[0]\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        kind = \"int\" if self.is_int else \"float\"\n        return f\"Tensor(shape={self.shape}, {kind})\"\n\n    __str__ = __repr__\n\n    def __format__(self, spec):\n        return repr(self)\n\n    def __bool__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"a tensor has no truth value; use item()\")\n\n    def __float__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"use item() to read a scalar\")\n\n    __int__ = __index__ = __float__\n\n    def __iter__(self):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors are not iterable\")\n\n    def __array__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"tensors cannot be converted to arrays\")\n\n    __hash__ = object.__hash__\n\n    def item(self):\n        _train_only(\"item()\")\n        if self._d.size != 1:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"item() needs a one-element tensor\")\n        _M.items += 1\n        if _M.items > _M.item_cap:\n            raise RuleViolation(f\"more than {_M.item_cap} item() reads\")\n        _tick()\n        return self._d.item()\n\n    def detach(self):\n        return Tensor(self._d)\n\n    # ---- in-place update of a parameter (optimizers)\n    def update(self, value):\n        _train_only(\"update()\")\n        value = _as_tensor(value, self)\n        if value.shape != self.shape:\n            value = Tensor(_np.broadcast_to(value._d, self.shape))\n        _tick(self.size // 4)\n        self._d[...] = value._d\n\n    # ---- autodiff\n    def backward(self):\n        _train_only(\"backward()\")\n        if self.size != 1:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"backward() needs a scalar loss\")\n        order, seen, stack = [], set(), [(self, False)]\n        while stack:\n            node, done = stack.pop()\n            if done:\n                order.append(node)\n                continue\n            if id(node) in seen or not node._rg:\n                continue\n            seen.add(id(node))\n            stack.append((node, True))\n            for p in node._prev:\n                stack.append((p, False))\n        grads = {id(self): _np.ones_like(self._d)}\n        for node in reversed(order):\n            g = grads.pop(id(node), None)\n            if g is None:\n                continue\n            if node._back is None:\n                if node.grad is None:\n                    node.grad = Tensor(g.astype(_F, copy=False))\n                else:\n                    _tick(g.size // 4)\n                    node.grad._d = node.grad._d + g\n                continue\n            _tick()\n            need = [p._rg for p in node._prev]\n            for p, pg in zip(node._prev, node._back(g, need)):\n                if pg is None or not p._rg:\n                    continue\n                if id(p) in grads:\n                    _tick(pg.size // 4)\n                    grads[id(p)] = grads[id(p)] + pg\n                else:\n                    grads[id(p)] = pg\n            node._prev, node._back = (), None\n\n    # ---- operators\n    def __add__(self, o):\n        return add(self, o)\n\n    def __radd__(self, o):\n        return add(o, self)\n\n    def __sub__(self, o):\n        return sub(self, o)\n\n    def __rsub__(self, o):\n        return sub(o, self)\n\n    def __mul__(self, o):\n        return mul(self, o)\n\n    def __rmul__(self, o):\n        return mul(o, self)\n\n    def __truediv__(self, o):\n        return div(self, o)\n\n    def __rtruediv__(self, o):\n        return div(o, self)\n\n    def __neg__(self):\n        return neg(self)\n\n    def __pow__(self, p):\n        return power(self, p)\n\n    def __matmul__(self, o):\n        return matmul(self, o)\n\n    def __mod__(self, o):\n        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.mod, per_4=4)\n\n    def __floordiv__(self, o):\n        return _int_binary(self, o, _np.floor_divide, per_4=4)\n\n    def __gt__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater)\n\n    def __ge__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.greater_equal)\n\n    def __lt__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.less)\n\n    def __le__(self, o):\n        return _compare(self, o, _np.less_equal)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, key):\n        return getitem(self, key)\n\n    def reshape(self, *shape):\n        return reshape(self, *shape)\n\n    def transpose(self, *axes):\n        return transpose(self, *axes)\n\n    def swapaxes(self, a, b):\n        return swapaxes(self, a, b)\n\n    def sum(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return sum(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def mean(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return mean(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def max(self, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n        return max(self, axis, keepdims)\n\n    def float(self):\n        return to_float(self)\n\n    @property\n    def T(self):\n        return swapaxes(self, -1, -2)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n\n\ndef _as_tensor(x, like=None):\n    if isinstance(x, Tensor):\n        return x\n    if isinstance(x, bool) or not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n        raise RuleViolation(f\"expected a tensor or a number, got {type(x).__name__}\")\n    dtype = _I if (like is not None and like.is_int and isinstance(x, int)) else _F\n    return Tensor(_np.asarray(x, dtype=dtype))\n\n\ndef _make(d, parents, back):\n    rg = _M.grad and any(p._rg for p in parents)\n    return Tensor(d, parents if rg else (), back if rg else None, rg)\n\n\ndef _unbroadcast(g, shape):\n    if g.shape == shape:\n        return g\n    _tick(g.size // 4)\n    while g.ndim > len(shape):\n        g = g.sum(0)\n    axes = tuple(i for i, s in enumerate(shape) if s == 1 and g.shape[i] != 1)\n    return g.sum(axes, keepdims=True) if axes else g\n\n\ndef _floats(*ts):\n    for t in ts:\n        if t.is_int:\n            raise RuleViolation(\"this op needs float tensors; convert with .float()\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- creation\n\n\ndef param(x):\n    \"\"\"Mark a tensor as a trainable leaf.\"\"\"\n    _train_only(\"param()\")\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n    t = Tensor(_np.array(x._d, dtype=_F))\n    t._rg = True\n    return t\n\n\ndef zeros(shape):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 16)\n    return Tensor(_np.zeros(shape, _F))\n\n\ndef ones(shape):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n    return Tensor(_np.ones(shape, _F))\n\n\ndef full(shape, value):\n    _tick(_np.prod(shape) // 8)\n    return Tensor(_np.full(shape, float(value), _F))\n\n\ndef arange(n):\n    _tick(n // 4)\n    return Tensor(_np.arange(n, dtype=_F))\n\n\ndef randn(shape, std=1.0):\n    _train_only(\"randn()\")\n    _tick(4 * _np.prod(shape))\n    return Tensor((_M.init_rng.standard_normal(shape, dtype=_F) * _F(std)).astype(_F))\n\n\ndef rand(shape):\n    _train_only(\"rand()\")\n    _tick(2 * _np.prod(shape))\n    return Tensor(_M.init_rng.random(shape, dtype=_F))\n\n\ndef tril(x, k=0):\n    \"\"\"Zero the elements above the k-th diagonal of the last two axes.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    keep = _np.tril(_np.ones(x.shape[-2:], dtype=bool), k)\n    out = _np.where(keep, x._d, _F(0))\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(2 * g.size)\n        return (_np.where(keep, g, _F(0)),)\n\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef where(mask, a, b):\n    \"\"\"mask is a float tensor of zeros and ones (from a comparison or tril).\"\"\"\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(mask, a, b)\n    m = mask._d != 0\n    out = _np.where(m, a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n    _tick(2 * out.size)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(2 * g.size)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, g, _F(0)), a.shape)\n        if need[2]:\n            _tick(2 * g.size)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(_np.where(m, _F(0), g), b.shape)\n        return (None, ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (mask, a, b), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elementwise\n\n\ndef _unary(x, f, df, fwd=4, bwd=1):\n    \"\"\"df(x_array, out_array, g) -> grad. fwd and bwd are prices in ticks per 4 elements.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(x.size * fwd // 4)\n    xd = x._d\n    out = f(xd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(g.size * bwd // 4)\n        return (df(xd, out, g),)\n\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef neg(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.negative, lambda x, y, g: -g, fwd=1)\n\n\ndef exp(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.exp, lambda x, y, g: g * y)\n\n\ndef log(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.log, lambda x, y, g: g / x, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef sqrt(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.sqrt, lambda x, y, g: g * _F(0.5) / y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef rsqrt(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / _np.sqrt(a), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(-0.5) * y * y * y, fwd=2, bwd=2)\n\n\ndef tanh(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.tanh, lambda x, y, g: g * (1 - y * y), fwd=2, bwd=4)\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: 1 / (1 + _np.exp(-a)), lambda x, y, g: g * y * (1 - y), bwd=2)\n\n\ndef relu(x):\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.maximum(a, _F(0)), lambda x, y, g: g * (x > 0), fwd=2)\n\n\ndef sin(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.sin, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.cos(x), bwd=4)\n\n\ndef cos(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.cos, lambda x, y, g: -g * _np.sin(x), bwd=4)\n\n\ndef abs(x):\n    return _unary(x, _np.abs, lambda x, y, g: g * _np.sign(x), fwd=1, bwd=8)\n\n\ndef sign(x):\n    \"\"\"No gradient.\"\"\"\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(x.size * 2)\n    return Tensor(_np.sign(x._d).astype(_F))\n\n\ndef power(x, p):\n    if not isinstance(p, (int, float)) or isinstance(p, bool):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"power() takes a number exponent\")\n    return _unary(x, lambda a: _np.power(a, _F(p)), lambda x, y, g: g * _F(p) * _np.power(x, _F(p - 1)), fwd=8, bwd=8)\n\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.add)\n    out = a._d + b._d\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, _unbroadcast(g, b.shape) if need[1] else None)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef sub(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.subtract)\n    out = a._d - b._d\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        gb = None\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(-g, b.shape)\n        return (_unbroadcast(g, a.shape) if need[0] else None, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef mul(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a, b if isinstance(b, Tensor) else None), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if a.is_int or b.is_int:\n        return _int_binary(a, b, _np.multiply)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    out = ad * bd\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g * bd, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ad, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef div(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(a, b)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    out = (ad / bd).astype(_F, copy=False)\n    _tick(out.size // 2)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 2)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g / bd, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(-g * out / bd, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef maximum(a, b):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b)\n    _floats(a, b)\n    out = _np.maximum(a._d, b._d)\n    _tick(out.size // 2)\n    pick_a = a._d >= b._d\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            ga = _unbroadcast(g * pick_a, a.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(g.size // 4)\n            gb = _unbroadcast(g * ~pick_a, b.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\ndef minimum(a, b):\n    return neg(maximum(neg(a), neg(b)))\n\n\ndef _compare(a, b, f):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_F)\n    _tick(out.size // 4)\n    return Tensor(out)\n\n\ndef _int_binary(a, b, f, per_4=1):\n    a, b = _as_tensor(a), _as_tensor(b, a)\n    if not (a.is_int and b.is_int):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"integer ops need two integer operands\")\n    out = f(a._d, b._d).astype(_I)\n    _tick(out.size * per_4 // 4)\n    return Tensor(out)\n\n\ndef to_float(x):\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n    return Tensor(x._d.astype(_F))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reductions\n\n\ndef _norm_axis(axis, ndim):\n    if axis is None:\n        return tuple(range(ndim))\n    axes = axis if isinstance(axis, tuple) else (axis,)\n    return tuple(a % ndim for a in axes)\n\n\ndef sum(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    _floats(x)\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    out = x._d.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=keepdims, dtype=_F)\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size // 8)\n        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n        return (_np.broadcast_to(gk, x.shape).astype(_F),)\n\n    return _make(_np.asarray(out, _F), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef mean(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    n = int(_np.prod([x.shape[a] for a in axes]))\n    return mul(sum(x, axis, keepdims), 1.0 / n)\n\n\ndef max(x, axis=None, keepdims=False):\n    _floats(x)\n    axes = _norm_axis(axis, x.ndim)\n    out = x._d.max(axis=axes, keepdims=True)\n    _tick(x.size // 4)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        gk = g if keepdims else _np.expand_dims(g, axes)\n        hit = x._d == out\n        return (hit * gk / hit.sum(axis=axes, keepdims=True),)\n\n    return _make(out if keepdims else out.squeeze(axes), (x,), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shapes (views are free)\n\n\ndef _reshaped(a, shape):\n    out = a.reshape(shape)\n    _tick(0 if _np.may_share_memory(out, a) else out.size)\n    return out\n\n\ndef reshape(x, *shape):\n    if len(shape) == 1 and isinstance(shape[0], tuple):\n        shape = shape[0]\n    src = x.shape\n    return _make(_reshaped(x._d, shape), (x,), lambda g, need: (_reshaped(g, src),))\n\n\ndef transpose(x, *axes):\n    if len(axes) == 1 and isinstance(axes[0], tuple):\n        axes = axes[0]\n    axes = axes or tuple(reversed(range(x.ndim)))\n    inv = tuple(_np.argsort(axes))\n    _tick()\n    return _make(x._d.transpose(axes), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.transpose(inv),))\n\n\ndef swapaxes(x, a, b):\n    _tick()\n    return _make(x._d.swapaxes(a, b), (x,), lambda g, need: (g.swapaxes(a, b),))\n\n\ndef _check_basic_key(key):\n    keys = key if isinstance(key, tuple) else (key,)\n    for k in keys:\n        if type(k) not in (int, slice, type(None), type(...)):\n            raise RuleViolation(\"indexing takes ints, slices, None and ...; use embedding() to gather\")\n\n\ndef getitem(x, key):\n    _check_basic_key(key)\n    _tick()\n    out = x._d[key]\n    src_shape = x.shape\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(_np.prod(src_shape) // 16 + g.size // 4)\n        full_g = _np.zeros(src_shape, _F)\n        full_g[key] = g\n        return (full_g,)\n\n    if x.is_int:\n        return Tensor(out)\n    return _make(out, (x,), back)\n\n\ndef split(x, sections, axis=-1):\n    \"\"\"Split into equal parts (a view; the backward is a concat).\"\"\"\n    parts = _np.split(x._d, sections, axis=axis)\n    _tick(_CALL * len(parts))\n    outs = []\n    for i, part in enumerate(parts):\n\n        def back(g, need, i=i):\n            _tick(_np.prod(x.shape) // 4 + 512 * len(parts))\n            full_g = [_np.zeros_like(p) for p in parts]\n            full_g[i] = g\n            return (_np.concatenate(full_g, axis=axis),)\n\n        outs.append(_make(part, (x,), back) if not x.is_int else Tensor(part))\n    return outs\n\n\ndef concat(ts, axis=-1):\n    ts = list(ts)\n    out = _np.concatenate([t._d for t in ts], axis=axis)\n    _tick(out.size // 4 + 256 * len(ts))\n    if all(t.is_int for t in ts):\n        return Tensor(out)\n    _floats(*ts)\n    bounds = _np.cumsum([t.shape[axis] for t in ts])[:-1]\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(1024 * len(ts))\n        return tuple(_np.split(g, bounds, axis=axis))\n\n    return _make(out, tuple(ts), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- matmul\n\n\ndef _matmul_price(rows, inner, cols, calls):\n    # thin products run far below BLAS's peak rate, so short sides price as if they had 8 rows or columns and 64 inner\n    return calls * ((rows if rows > 8 else 8) * (cols if cols > 8 else 8) * (inner if inner > 64 else 64) // 128 + 256)\n\n\ndef matmul(a, b):\n    _floats(a, b)\n    ad, bd = a._d, b._d\n    if ad.ndim < 2 or bd.ndim < 2:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"matmul() needs tensors with at least two dimensions\")\n    m, k, n = ad.shape[-2], ad.shape[-1], bd.shape[-1]\n    calls = int(_np.prod(_np.broadcast_shapes(ad.shape[:-2], bd.shape[:-2])))\n    if bd.ndim == 2:\n        m, calls = m * calls, 1\n    _tick(_matmul_price(m, k, n, calls))  # before the work, because time here is not bounded by memory\n    if bd.ndim == 2 and ad.ndim > 2:\n        lead = ad.shape[:-1]\n        out = (ad.reshape(-1, ad.shape[-1]) @ bd).reshape(*lead, bd.shape[-1])\n    else:\n        out = ad @ bd\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        ga = gb = None\n        if need[0]:\n            _tick(_matmul_price(m, n, k, calls))\n            if bd.ndim == 2:\n                ga = (g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1]) @ bd.T).reshape(ad.shape)\n            else:\n                ga = _unbroadcast(g @ _np.swapaxes(bd, -1, -2), ad.shape)\n        if need[1]:\n            _tick(_matmul_price(k, m, n, calls))\n            if bd.ndim == 2:\n                gb = ad.reshape(-1, k).T @ g.reshape(-1, g.shape[-1])\n            else:\n                gb = _unbroadcast(_np.swapaxes(ad, -1, -2) @ g, bd.shape)\n        return (ga, gb)\n\n    return _make(out, (a, b), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- indexing\n\n\ndef embedding(table, idx):\n    \"\"\"Rows of a 2-D table picked by an integer tensor: out[...] = table[idx[...]].\"\"\"\n    _floats(table)\n    if not idx.is_int:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding() needs an integer index tensor\")\n    ix = idx._d\n    if ix.size and (ix.min() < 0 or ix.max() >= table.shape[0]):\n        raise RuleViolation(\"embedding index out of range\")\n    out = table._d[ix]\n    _tick((8 + table.size // (1 << 19)) * ix.size + out.size // 4)  # bigger tables miss the cache on more rows\n    rows = table.shape\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(16 * g.size + table.size // 16)\n        gt = _np.zeros(rows, _F)\n        _np.add.at(gt, ix.reshape(-1), g.reshape(-1, rows[1]))\n        return (gt, None)\n\n    return _make(out, (table, idx), back)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fused\n\n\ndef softmax(x, axis=-1):\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n    e = _np.exp(z)\n    y = e / e.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        return (y * (g - (g * y).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True)),)\n\n    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef log_softmax(x, axis=-1):\n    _floats(x)\n    _tick(2 * x.size)\n    z = x._d - x._d.max(axis=axis, keepdims=True)\n    lse = _np.log(_np.exp(z).sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True))\n    y = z - lse\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(x.size)\n        return (g - _np.exp(y) * g.sum(axis=axis, keepdims=True),)\n\n    return _make(y.astype(_F, copy=False), (x,), back)\n\n\ndef cross_entropy(logits, targets):\n    \"\"\"Mean negative log-likelihood in nats. logits (..., V) float, targets (...) int.\"\"\"\n    _floats(logits)\n    if not targets.is_int:\n        raise RuleViolation(\"cross_entropy() needs integer targets\")\n    V = logits.shape[-1]\n    z = logits._d.reshape(-1, V)\n    t = targets._d.reshape(-1)\n    _tick(2 * z.size + _CALL)\n    zmax = z.max(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    e = _np.exp(z - zmax)\n    s = e.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    n = z.shape[0]\n    nll = (_np.log(s[:, 0]) + zmax[:, 0] - z[_np.arange(n), t]).mean()\n\n    def back(g, need):\n        _tick(z.size)\n        p = e / s\n        p[_np.arange(n), t] -= 1\n        return ((p * (g / n)).reshape(logits.shape).astype(_F, copy=False), None)\n\n    return _make(_np.asarray(nll, _F), (logits, targets), back)\n", "numLines": 867, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 867}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01L3QjvhH5ydkF7o1cWRW1Sk", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Xfa4kB6UAbC2VYKdeBm3Hw", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1\t\"\"\"Rerun an entry on fresh seeds and score it. This file is the referee.\n2\t\n3\t    python verify.py entries/gpt/train.py                         # 8 fresh seeds, scored on the test split\n4\t    python verify.py entries/gpt/train.py --seeds 2               # 2 fresh seeds\n5\t    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --seeds 11,12 --split dev\n6\t    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --against records/current.json\n7\t    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --smoke                # seconds, for checking that an entry runs\n8\t\n9\tWhat a run guarantees:\n10\t  1. The source passes static rules. It imports only odometer and math, and it can name only the engine's public API,\n11\t     math, and plain container methods. No try, class, global, match, decorator or attribute assignment (except\n12\t     x.grad = None), and no module-level state beyond constants. Literals and syntax nodes are rationed, so a table\n13\t     cannot be smuggled in the source.\n14\t  2. train() runs in its own process with one BLAS thread, under the training budget, with the verifier's seed. That\n15\t     process never loads held-out bytes. A run that lets BudgetExhausted escape is void.\n16\t  3. Python work outside the engine is counted, not timed: entry lines and jumps are capped. One C call counts once\n17\t     however long it runs (a sum over a long range, big-integer arithmetic); that work has only the rationed item()\n18\t     reads to learn from, and the wall limit ends it.\n19\t  4. Scoring runs in a second, fresh process. forward() sees held-out inputs, never targets, and its compute per byte\n20\t     is capped. Every call gets a fresh params dict and fresh tensors, so no state survives between calls. A quarter\n21\t     of the windows get a twin whose bytes after a random cut come from another window; a shuffle puts nearly all twins\n22\t     in other batches. Logits before the cut must match, which catches forward() looking ahead or across rows.\n23\t  5. Seeds are drawn fresh unless given, and written to the log, so anyone can rerun the exact runs.\n24\t\"\"\"\n25\t\n26\timport argparse\n27\timport ast\n28\timport builtins\n29\timport hashlib\n30\timport json\n31\timport math\n32\timport os\n33\timport pathlib\n34\timport platform\n35\timport secrets\n36\timport subprocess\n37\timport sys\n38\timport tempfile\n39\timport time\n40\timport types\n41\tfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n42\t\n43\tROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n44\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n45\t\n46\timport stats  # noqa: E402\n47\t\n48\tTRACK = {\n49\t    \"version\": \"odometer-v3\",\n50\t    \"train_budget\": 40_000_000_000,  # ticks for everything train() does; about 80 s on a 4-core VM, 25 s on an M4\n51\t    \"eval_ticks_per_byte\": 50_000,  # forward() price cap per scored byte\n52\t    \"param_cap\": 1 << 22,  # floats in the returned parameters, plus characters in their names\n53\t    \"source_cap\": 64 * 1024,  # bytes of train.py\n54\t    \"literal_cap\": 4096,  # bytes of literals, keyword names and function names in train.py\n55\t    \"node_cap\": 8192,  # syntax nodes in train.py; a table spelled in variable names has no literals to count\n56\t    \"python_lines\": 20_000_000,  # entry lines and jumps per process\n57\t    \"eval_context\": 512,\n58\t    \"eval_batch\": 16,\n59\t    \"eval_windows\": 1024,  # windows of eval_context bytes per held-out split\n60\t    \"twin_fraction\": 0.25,\n61\t    \"twin_positions\": 32,\n62\t    \"twin_tolerance\": 1e-4,  # max |log p| difference between twins, in nats; a leak this small gains 1.4e-4 bits per byte\n63\t    \"item_cap\": 20_000,  # item() reads in train()\n64\t    \"wall_limit_seconds\": 3600,  # only catches hangs; it never decides a score\n65\t}\n66\tSMOKE = {\"train_budget\": 2_000_000_000, \"eval_windows\": 32, \"wall_limit_seconds\": 300}\n67\tRECORD_ALPHA = 0.01\n68\tRECORD_MARGIN = 0.002  # bits per byte a new record must clear on top of the significance test\n69\tLOW_VARIANCE_RATIO = 0.3  # seed SD below this fraction of the incumbent's gets flagged for a human look\n70\tTHREAD_VARS = (\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", \"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\", \"MKL_NUM_THREADS\", \"VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS\", \"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\")\n71\t\n72\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- static rules\n73\t\n74\tALLOWED_IMPORTS = {\"odometer\", \"math\"}\n75\tALLOWED_BUILTINS = {\n76\t    \"abs\", \"all\", \"any\", \"bool\", \"dict\", \"divmod\", \"enumerate\", \"float\", \"int\", \"isinstance\", \"len\", \"list\", \"max\",\n77\t    \"min\", \"pow\", \"print\", \"range\", \"reversed\", \"round\", \"set\", \"sorted\", \"str\", \"sum\", \"tuple\", \"zip\",\n78\t    \"True\", \"False\", \"None\",\n79\t}\n80\t# math without its functions over sequences and big integers, which do unbounded numeric work in one counted line\n81\tMATH_NAMES = {n for n in dir(math) if not n.startswith(\"_\")} - {\n82\t    \"comb\", \"dist\", \"factorial\", \"fsum\", \"gcd\", \"hypot\", \"isqrt\", \"lcm\", \"perm\", \"prod\", \"sumprod\",\n83\t}\n84\tCONTAINER_ATTRS = {\n85\t    \"append\", \"extend\", \"insert\", \"pop\", \"remove\", \"reverse\", \"sort\", \"index\", \"count\", \"clear\", \"copy\", \"items\", \"keys\",\n86\t    \"values\", \"get\", \"setdefault\", \"update\", \"join\", \"split\", \"strip\", \"startswith\", \"endswith\",\n87\t}\n88\tBANNED_NODES = (\n89\t    ast.ClassDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef, ast.AsyncFor, ast.AsyncWith, ast.Await, ast.Try, ast.TryStar, ast.Match,\n90\t    ast.Global, ast.Nonlocal, ast.Delete, ast.TypeAlias,\n91\t)\n92\t\n93\t\n94\tdef allowed_attrs():\n95\t    import odometer as od\n96\t\n97\t    engine = {n for n in dir(od) if not n.startswith(\"_\")} - {\"Tensor\"}\n98\t    tensor = {n for n in dir(od.Tensor) if not n.startswith(\"_\")}\n99\t    return engine, engine | tensor | {\"batch\", \"num_bytes\"} | MATH_NAMES | CONTAINER_ATTRS\n100\t\n101\t\n102\tdef is_constant_expr(node):\n103\t    return all(isinstance(n, (ast.Constant, ast.Tuple, ast.UnaryOp, ast.BinOp, ast.Name, ast.Load, ast.operator, ast.unaryop))\n104\t               for n in ast.walk(node))\n105\t\n106\t\n107\tdef literal_bytes(tree):\n108\t    \"\"\"Everything in the source an entry can read back as data. dict(name=1) and str(function) turn names into strings.\"\"\"\n109\t    docstrings = {id(n.body[0].value) for n in ast.walk(tree)\n110\t                  if isinstance(n, (ast.Module, ast.FunctionDef)) and n.body and isinstance(n.body[0], ast.Expr)\n111\t                  and isinstance(n.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(n.body[0].value.value, str)}\n112\t\n113\t    def size(v):\n114\t        if isinstance(v, str):\n115\t            return len(v.encode(\"utf-8\", \"surrogatepass\"))\n116\t        return len(v) if isinstance(v, bytes) else max(8, v.bit_length() // 8) if isinstance(v, int) else 8\n117\t\n118\t    total = 0\n119\t    for n in ast.walk(tree):\n120\t        if isinstance(n, ast.Constant) and id(n) not in docstrings:\n121\t            total += size(n.value)\n122\t        elif isinstance(n, ast.keyword) and n.arg:\n123\t            total += size(n.arg)\n124\t        elif isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef):\n125\t            total += size(n.name)\n126\t    return total\n127\t\n128\t\n129\tdef static_problems(src, track=TRACK):\n130\t    if len(src.encode()) > track[\"source_cap\"]:\n131\t        return [f\"source is over {track['source_cap']} bytes\"]\n132\t    try:\n133\t        tree = ast.parse(src)\n134\t    except (SyntaxError, MemoryError, RecursionError) as e:\n135\t        return [f\"syntax error: {e}\"]\n136\t    engine, attrs = allowed_attrs()\n137\t    forbidden = set(dir(builtins)) - ALLOWED_BUILTINS\n138\t    nodes = list(ast.walk(tree))\n139\t    clears_grad = {id(t) for n in nodes if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and isinstance(n.value, ast.Constant) and n.value.value is None\n140\t                   for t in n.targets if isinstance(t, ast.Attribute) and t.attr == \"grad\"}\n141\t    problems = []\n142\t    for node in nodes:\n143\t        line = getattr(node, \"lineno\", 0)\n144\t        if isinstance(node, BANNED_NODES):\n145\t            problems.append(f\"line {line}: {type(node).__name__} is not allowed\")\n146\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.Import):\n147\t            problems += [f\"line {line}: import {a.name}\" for a in node.names if a.name not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS]\n148\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom):\n149\t            if node.level or node.module not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS:\n150\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: from {'.' * node.level}{node.module or ''} import\")\n151\t            else:\n152\t                names = engine if node.module == \"odometer\" else MATH_NAMES\n153\t                problems += [f\"line {line}: from {node.module} import {a.name}\" for a in node.names if a.name not in names]\n154\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.alias):\n155\t            if node.asname and node.asname.startswith(\"_\"):  # import math as __builtins__ swaps the builtins table\n156\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.asname} starts with an underscore\")\n157\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.Attribute):\n158\t            if node.attr not in attrs:\n159\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: .{node.attr} is not on the allowed list\")\n160\t            if not isinstance(node.ctx, ast.Load) and id(node) not in clears_grad:\n161\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: assigning to .{node.attr}\")\n162\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.Name):\n163\t            if node.id.startswith(\"_\") and node.id != \"_\":\n164\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.id} starts with an underscore\")\n165\t            elif node.id in forbidden:\n166\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: builtin {node.id} is not on the allowed list\")\n167\t        elif isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.Lambda)):\n168\t            if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef):\n169\t                if node.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n170\t                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.name} starts with an underscore\")\n171\t                if node.decorator_list:  # a decorator is a call at module level, so it could build state that persists\n172\t                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: decorators are not allowed\")\n173\t                if node.returns and not is_constant_expr(node.returns):\n174\t                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: an annotation must be a constant\")\n175\t            if not all(is_constant_expr(d) for d in [*node.args.defaults, *node.args.kw_defaults] if d is not None):\n176\t                problems.append(f\"line {line}: a default argument must be a constant\")\n177\t        elif isinstance(node, ast.arg) and node.annotation and not is_constant_expr(node.annotation):\n178\t            problems.append(f\"line {line}: an annotation must be a constant\")  # annotations run once, at def time\n179\t    for node in tree.body:\n180\t        fine = isinstance(node, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom, ast.FunctionDef))\n181\t        fine |= isinstance(node, ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.value, ast.Constant)\n182\t        fine |= (isinstance(node, ast.Assign) and all(isinstance(t, ast.Name) for t in node.targets) and is_constant_expr(node.value))\n183\t        if not fine:\n184\t            problems.append(f\"line {node.lineno}: module level allows only imports, defs and constants\")\n185\t    if literal_bytes(tree) > track[\"literal_cap\"]:\n186\t        problems.append(f\"literals total {literal_bytes(tree)} bytes, over the cap of {track['literal_cap']}\")\n187\t    if len(nodes) > track[\"node_cap\"]:\n188\t        problems.append(f\"source has {len(nodes)} syntax nodes, over the cap of {track['node_cap']}\")\n189\t    top = {n.name for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef)}\n190\t    problems += [f\"no top-level {f}()\" for f in (\"train\", \"forward\") if f not in top]\n191\t    return problems\n192\t\n193\t\n194\tdef load_entry(path, track):\n195\t    \"\"\"Execute the entry with a builtins table that has no way out of the engine.\"\"\"\n196\t    src = pathlib.Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n197\t    problems = static_problems(src, track)\n198\t    if problems:\n199\t        raise SystemExit(\"static rules failed:\\n  \" + \"\\n  \".join(problems))\n200\t\n201\t    def guarded_import(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0):\n202\t        if level or name not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS:\n203\t            raise ImportError(f\"import of {name} is not allowed\")\n204\t        return builtins.__import__(name, globals, locals, fromlist, level)\n205\t\n206\t    safe = {k: getattr(builtins, k) for k in ALLOWED_BUILTINS}\n207\t    safe[\"__import__\"] = guarded_import\n208\t    module = types.ModuleType(\"entry\")\n209\t    module.__dict__[\"__builtins__\"] = safe\n210\t    exec(compile(src, str(path), \"exec\"), module.__dict__)\n211\t    return module\n212\t\n213\t\n214\tdef peak_rss_mb():\n215\t    import resource\n216\t\n217\t    kb = resource.getrusage(resource.RUSAGE_SELF).ru_maxrss\n218\t    return kb / 1024 ** (2 if sys.platform == \"darwin\" else 1)\n219\t\n220\t\n221\tdef count_python_work(entry, cap, violation):\n222\t    \"\"\"Deterministic fence on Python outside the engine: every line and jump of the entry costs one count.\"\"\"\n223\t    mon, events = sys.monitoring, sys.monitoring.events\n224\t    seen = [0]\n225\t\n226\t    def on_event(code, *rest):\n227\t        if code.co_filename != entry:\n228\t            return mon.DISABLE\n229\t        seen[0] += 1\n230\t        if seen[0] > cap:\n231\t            raise violation(f\"more than {cap} Python lines and jumps in the entry\")\n232\t\n233\t    mon.use_tool_id(mon.PROFILER_ID, \"odometer\")\n234\t    mon.register_callback(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.LINE, on_event)\n235\t    mon.register_callback(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.JUMP, on_event)\n236\t    mon.set_events(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.LINE | events.JUMP)\n237\t    return seen\n238\t\n239\t\n240\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the two child processes\n241\t\n242\t\n243\tdef child_train(entry, seed, out):\n244\t    import numpy as np\n245\t\n246\t    import odometer as od\n247\t    from odometer import _data, _engine\n248\t\n249\t    out = pathlib.Path(out)\n250\t    track = json.loads((out / \"track.json\").read_text())\n251\t    _engine._M.reset(track[\"train_budget\"], seed, item_cap=track[\"item_cap\"])\n252\t    data = _data.TrainData()\n253\t    lines = count_python_work(entry, track[\"python_lines\"], od.RuleViolation)\n254\t    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n255\t    status, params = \"ok\", None\n256\t    try:\n257\t        params = load_entry(entry, track).train(data)\n258\t    except od.BudgetExhausted as e:\n259\t        status = f\"void: BudgetExhausted escaped train() ({e})\"\n260\t    except od.RuleViolation as e:\n261\t        status = f\"void: rule violation: {e}\"\n262\t    seconds = time.perf_counter() - t0\n263\t    sys.monitoring.set_events(sys.monitoring.PROFILER_ID, 0)\n264\t    if status == \"ok\":\n265\t        if not isinstance(params, dict) or not all(isinstance(k, str) and type(v) is od.Tensor for k, v in params.items()):\n266\t            status = \"void: train() must return a dict of name -> Tensor\"\n267\t        elif any(v.is_int for v in params.values()):\n268\t            status = \"void: parameters must be float tensors\"\n269\t        elif sum(v.size + len(k) for k, v in params.items()) > track[\"param_cap\"]:\n270\t            status = f\"void: more than {track['param_cap']} parameters, with one more per character of their names\"\n271\t        else:\n272\t            np.savez(out / \"params.npz\", **{f\"p{i}\": v._d for i, v in enumerate(params.values())})\n273\t            (out / \"names.json\").write_text(json.dumps(list(params)))\n274\t    report = {\"status\": status, \"train_ticks\": _engine._M.used, \"train_seconds\": seconds, \"item_reads\": _engine._M.items,\n275\t              \"train_python_lines\": lines[0], \"peak_rss_mb\": peak_rss_mb(), \"params\": sum(v.size for v in params.values()) if status == \"ok\" else None}\n276\t    (out / \"train.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report))\n277\t\n278\t\n279\tdef child_eval(entry, seed, split, out):\n280\t    import numpy as np\n281\t\n282\t    import odometer as od\n283\t    from odometer import _data, _engine\n284\t\n285\t    out = pathlib.Path(out)\n286\t    track = json.loads((out / \"track.json\").read_text())\n287\t    C, B = track[\"eval_context\"], track[\"eval_batch\"]\n288\t    windows = _data.heldout_windows(split, C, track[\"eval_windows\"])\n289\t    n = len(windows)\n290\t    rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 2])\n291\t    twins = np.sort(rng.choice(n, int(n * track[\"twin_fraction\"]), replace=False))\n292\t    cuts = rng.integers(1, C, size=twins.size)\n293\t    donors = windows[rng.integers(0, n, size=twins.size)]\n294\t    rows = np.concatenate([windows[:, :C], windows[twins, :C]])\n295\t    probe = []\n296\t    for j, (cut, donor) in enumerate(zip(cuts, donors)):\n297\t        rows[n + j, cut:] = donor[cut:C]\n298\t        last = np.arange(max(0, cut - 8), cut)  # a look-ahead leak shows first just before the cut\n299\t        probe.append(np.union1d(last, rng.choice(cut, min(cut, track[\"twin_positions\"]), replace=False)))\n300\t    probe_rows = {int(r): j for j, r in enumerate(twins)} | {n + j: j for j in range(twins.size)}\n301\t    order = rng.permutation(len(rows))\n302\t\n303\t    scored_bytes = len(rows) * C\n304\t    _engine._M.reset(track[\"eval_ticks_per_byte\"] * scored_bytes, seed, mode=\"eval\")\n305\t    lines = count_python_work(entry, track[\"python_lines\"], od.RuleViolation)\n306\t    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n307\t    status = \"ok\"\n308\t    nll = np.zeros(n)\n309\t    seen = {}\n310\t    try:\n311\t        module = load_entry(entry, track)\n312\t        names = json.loads((out / \"names.json\").read_text())\n313\t        stored = np.load(out / \"params.npz\")\n314\t        arrays = {name: stored[f\"p{i}\"] for i, name in enumerate(names)}\n315\t        for a in arrays.values():\n316\t            a.setflags(write=False)\n317\t        for start in range(0, len(rows), B):\n318\t            idx = order[start : start + B]\n319\t            logits = module.forward({k: od.Tensor(a) for k, a in arrays.items()}, od.Tensor(rows[idx].astype(np.int32)))\n320\t            if type(logits) is not od.Tensor or logits.is_int or logits.shape != (len(idx), C, od.VOCAB):\n321\t                raise od.RuleViolation(f\"forward() must return float logits of shape (batch, {C}, {od.VOCAB})\")\n322\t            z = logits._d.astype(np.float64)\n323\t            if not np.isfinite(z).all():\n324\t                raise od.RuleViolation(\"forward() returned non-finite logits\")\n325\t            lp = z - z.max(-1, keepdims=True)\n326\t            lp -= np.log(np.exp(lp).sum(-1, keepdims=True))\n327\t            for b, r in enumerate(idx):\n328\t                if r < n:\n329\t                    nll[r] = -lp[b, np.arange(C), windows[r, 1:]].sum()\n330\t                if int(r) in probe_rows:\n331\t                    j = probe_rows[int(r)]\n332\t                    seen.setdefault(j, []).append(lp[b, probe[j]])\n333\t    except od.BudgetExhausted:\n334\t        status = f\"void: forward() cost more than {track['eval_ticks_per_byte']:,} ticks per byte\"\n335\t    except od.RuleViolation as e:\n336\t        status = f\"void: rule violation: {e}\"\n337\t    sys.monitoring.set_events(sys.monitoring.PROFILER_ID, 0)\n338\t    twin_diff = max((float(np.abs(a - b).max()) for a, b in seen.values()), default=0.0) if status == \"ok\" else None\n339\t    if status == \"ok\" and twin_diff > track[\"twin_tolerance\"]:\n340\t        status = f\"void: twin check failed (logits before the cut moved by {twin_diff:.2e} nats)\"\n341\t    report = {\"status\": status, \"split\": split, \"bpb\": float(nll.sum() / (n * C) / np.log(2)) if status == \"ok\" else None,\n342\t              \"eval_ticks_per_byte\": _engine._M.used / scored_bytes, \"twin_max_diff\": twin_diff,\n343\t              \"eval_python_lines\": lines[0], \"eval_seconds\": time.perf_counter() - t0}\n344\t    (out / \"eval.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report))\n345\t\n346\t\n347\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the parent\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tdef run_seed(entry, seed, split, track, keep):\n351\t    env = {\"PATH\": os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"\"), **{v: \"1\" for v in THREAD_VARS}}\n352\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n353\t        (pathlib.Path(tmp) / \"track.json\").write_text(json.dumps(track))\n354\t        result = {\"seed\": seed}\n355\t        for stage, extra in ((\"train\", []), (\"eval\", [split])):\n356\t            cmd = [sys.executable, \"-I\", str(ROOT / \"verify.py\"), f\"--child-{stage}\", str(entry), str(seed), *extra, tmp]\n357\t            log = keep / f\"seed-{seed}-{stage}.log\"\n358\t            try:\n359\t                with open(log, \"wb\") as sink:\n360\t                    subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=tmp, env=env, stdout=sink, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=track[\"wall_limit_seconds\"])\n361\t            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n362\t                result[\"status\"] = f\"void: {stage} process passed the wall limit\"\n363\t                return result\n364\t            path = pathlib.Path(tmp) / f\"{stage}.json\"\n365\t            if not path.exists():\n366\t                result[\"status\"] = f\"void: {stage} process crashed (see {log.name})\"\n367\t                return result\n368\t            result |= json.loads(path.read_text())\n369\t            if result[\"status\"] != \"ok\":\n370\t                return result\n371\t        return result\n372\t\n373\t\n374\tdef machine():\n375\t    import numpy as np\n376\t\n377\t    blas = np.show_config(mode=\"dicts\")[\"Build Dependencies\"][\"blas\"]\n378\t    return {\"platform\": platform.platform(), \"machine\": platform.machine(), \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n379\t            \"numpy\": np.__version__, \"blas\": f\"{blas.get('name')} {blas.get('version')}\", \"cpus\": os.cpu_count()}\n380\t\n381\t\n382\tdef code_hash():\n383\t    h = hashlib.sha256()\n384\t    for p in [ROOT / \"verify.py\", *sorted((ROOT / \"odometer\").glob(\"*.py\"))]:\n385\t        h.update(p.read_bytes())\n386\t    return h.hexdigest()\n387\t\n388\t\n389\tdef run_batch(entry, seeds, split, track, logs, jobs, label=\"\"):\n390\t    with ThreadPoolExecutor(jobs) as pool:\n391\t        results = []\n392\t        for r in pool.map(lambda s: run_seed(entry, s, split, track, logs), seeds):\n393\t            results.append(r)\n394\t            if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\":\n395\t                print(f\"  seed {r['seed']:>10}  {split} bpb {r['bpb']:.4f}  train {r['train_ticks']:.3e} ticks  \"\n396\t                      f\"{r['train_seconds']:6.1f} s  eval {r['eval_ticks_per_byte']:,.0f} ticks/byte  \"\n397\t                      f\"twins {r['twin_max_diff']:.1e}{label}\", flush=True)\n398\t            else:\n399\t                print(f\"  seed {r['seed']:>10}  {r['status']}{label}\", flush=True)\n400\t    return results\n401\t\n402\t\n403\tdef fresh_seeds(n):\n404\t    return [secrets.randbits(31) for _ in range(n)]\n405\t\n406\t\n407\tdef judge(bpbs, record_bpbs):\n408\t    \"\"\"Does this batch beat the record by more than the margin? Welch, one-sided, on the verifier's own seeds.\"\"\"\n409\t    w = stats.welch(bpbs, [b - RECORD_MARGIN for b in record_bpbs])\n410\t    plain = stats.welch(bpbs, record_bpbs)\n411\t    return {\"gain\": -plain[\"diff\"], \"ci95\": plain[\"ci95\"], \"df\": w[\"df\"], \"p_beyond_margin\": w[\"p_one_sided\"],\n412\t            \"passes\": w[\"p_one_sided\"] < RECORD_ALPHA}\n413\t\n414\t\n415\tdef main():\n416\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n417\t    ap.add_argument(\"entry\")\n418\t    ap.add_argument(\"--seeds\", default=\"8\", help=\"a count of fresh seeds, or a comma list to rerun exact seeds ('11,' is seed 11)\")\n419\t    ap.add_argument(\"--split\", default=\"test\", choices=(\"dev\", \"test\"))\n420\t    ap.add_argument(\"--jobs\", type=int, default=0, help=\"seeds in parallel (default: min(seeds, cpus))\")\n421\t    ap.add_argument(\"--against\", help=\"a record log; tests whether this entry beats it, then confirms on new seeds\")\n422\t    ap.add_argument(\"--smoke\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"a tiny budget and a few windows; the number is not a score\")\n423\t    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", help=\"where to write the log (default runs/<entry>-<time>.json)\")\n424\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n425\t\n426\t    track = {**TRACK, **SMOKE} if args.smoke else TRACK\n427\t    entry = pathlib.Path(args.entry).resolve()\n428\t    src = entry.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n429\t    problems = static_problems(src, track)\n430\t    if problems:\n431\t        print(\"static rules failed:\\n  \" + \"\\n  \".join(problems))\n432\t        sys.exit(2)\n433\t    seeds = [int(s) for s in args.seeds.split(\",\") if s] if \",\" in args.seeds else fresh_seeds(int(args.seeds))\n434\t    name = entry.parent.name if entry.name == \"train.py\" else entry.stem\n435\t    stamp = time.strftime(\"%Y%m%d-%H%M%S\")\n436\t    out = pathlib.Path(args.out) if args.out else ROOT / \"runs\" / f\"{name}-{stamp}.json\"\n437\t    logs = out.with_suffix(\"\")\n438\t    logs.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n439\t    jobs = args.jobs or max(1, min(len(seeds), os.cpu_count() or 1))\n440\t    print(f\"{name}: {len(seeds)} seeds on {args.split}, {jobs} at a time, budget {track['train_budget']:.1e} ticks\"\n441\t          + (\" (smoke run: not a score)\" if args.smoke else \"\"), flush=True)\n442\t\n443\t    t0 = time.time()\n444\t    results = run_batch(entry, seeds, args.split, track, logs, jobs)\n445\t    ok = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in results if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\"]\n446\t    log = {\"entry\": str(entry.relative_to(ROOT)) if entry.is_relative_to(ROOT) else entry.name,\n447\t           \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(src.encode()).hexdigest(), \"code_sha256\": code_hash(), \"track\": track,\n448\t           \"split\": args.split, \"smoke\": args.smoke, \"machine\": machine(), \"started\": stamp, \"seeds\": results}\n449\t    if len(ok) == len(results) and len(ok) >= 2:\n450\t        m, half = stats.ci95(ok)\n451\t        log[\"summary\"] = {\"mean_bpb\": m, \"ci95\": half, \"sd\": stats.mean_sd(ok)[1], \"n\": len(ok)}\n452\t        print(f\"  mean {m:.4f} +- {half:.4f} bpb (95% CI, n={len(ok)}, sd {log['summary']['sd']:.4f})\")\n453\t    elif len(ok) != len(results):\n454\t        print(\"  void: at least one seed failed, so the entry has no score\")\n455\t    elif ok:\n456\t        print(f\"  {ok[0]:.4f} bpb on one seed (use at least 2 for an interval)\")\n457\t\n458\t    if args.against and \"summary\" in log:\n459\t        inc = json.loads(pathlib.Path(args.against).read_text())\n460\t        if inc[\"split\"] != args.split:\n461\t            raise SystemExit(\"the record was scored on a different split\")\n462\t        incumbent = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in inc.get(\"confirmation\", inc[\"seeds\"])]\n463\t        stage1 = judge(ok, incumbent)\n464\t        verdict = {\"against\": args.against, \"margin\": RECORD_MARGIN, \"alpha\": RECORD_ALPHA, \"stage1\": stage1, \"record\": False}\n465\t        print(f\"  gain over the record: {stage1['gain']:+.4f} +- {stage1['ci95']:.4f} bpb, p = {stage1['p_beyond_margin']:.2g} \"\n466\t              f\"(beyond a margin of {RECORD_MARGIN})\")\n467\t        if stats.mean_sd(ok)[1] < LOW_VARIANCE_RATIO * stats.mean_sd(incumbent)[1]:\n468\t            verdict[\"flag\"] = \"seed SD is far below the incumbent's; read the entry for a fixed init or data order\"\n469\t            print(f\"  flag: {verdict['flag']}\")\n470\t        if stage1[\"passes\"]:\n471\t            print(\"  passed; confirming on new seeds\", flush=True)\n472\t            second = run_batch(entry, fresh_seeds(len(seeds)), args.split, track, logs, jobs, label=\"  (confirmation)\")\n473\t            log[\"confirmation\"] = second\n474\t            good = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in second if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\"]\n475\t            if len(good) == len(second):\n476\t                stage2 = judge(good, incumbent)\n477\t                verdict[\"stage2\"] = stage2\n478\t                verdict[\"record\"] = stage2[\"passes\"]\n479\t                print(f\"  confirmation: {stage2['gain']:+.4f} +- {stage2['ci95']:.4f} bpb, p = {stage2['p_beyond_margin']:.2g}\")\n480\t        print(\"  NEW RECORD\" if verdict[\"record\"] else \"  not a record\")\n481\t        log[\"verdict\"] = verdict\n482\t    log[\"wall_seconds\"] = time.time() - t0\n483\t    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n484\t    out.write_text(json.dumps(log, indent=1))\n485\t    print(f\"  log: {out.relative_to(ROOT) if out.is_relative_to(ROOT) else out}\")\n486\t    if len(ok) != len(results):\n487\t        sys.exit(1)\n488\t\n489\t\n490\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n491\t    if len(sys.argv) > 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"--child-train\":\n492\t        child_train(sys.argv[2], int(sys.argv[3]), sys.argv[4])\n493\t    elif len(sys.argv) > 1 and sys.argv[1] == \"--child-eval\":\n494\t        child_eval(sys.argv[2], int(sys.argv[3]), sys.argv[4], sys.argv[5])\n495\t    else:\n496\t        main()\n497\t"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c1587825-b49a-4867-a7de-efec5b369583", "uuid": "5c89aaa9-ad20-494b-848b-b694f1d8996e", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T13:40:23.270Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/home/user/att/attempt-01/verify.py", "content": "\"\"\"Rerun an entry on fresh seeds and score it. This file is the referee.\n\n    python verify.py entries/gpt/train.py                         # 8 fresh seeds, scored on the test split\n    python verify.py entries/gpt/train.py --seeds 2               # 2 fresh seeds\n    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --seeds 11,12 --split dev\n    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --against records/current.json\n    python verify.py entries/mine/train.py --smoke                # seconds, for checking that an entry runs\n\nWhat a run guarantees:\n  1. The source passes static rules. It imports only odometer and math, and it can name only the engine's public API,\n     math, and plain container methods. No try, class, global, match, decorator or attribute assignment (except\n     x.grad = None), and no module-level state beyond constants. Literals and syntax nodes are rationed, so a table\n     cannot be smuggled in the source.\n  2. train() runs in its own process with one BLAS thread, under the training budget, with the verifier's seed. That\n     process never loads held-out bytes. A run that lets BudgetExhausted escape is void.\n  3. Python work outside the engine is counted, not timed: entry lines and jumps are capped. One C call counts once\n     however long it runs (a sum over a long range, big-integer arithmetic); that work has only the rationed item()\n     reads to learn from, and the wall limit ends it.\n  4. Scoring runs in a second, fresh process. forward() sees held-out inputs, never targets, and its compute per byte\n     is capped. Every call gets a fresh params dict and fresh tensors, so no state survives between calls. A quarter\n     of the windows get a twin whose bytes after a random cut come from another window; a shuffle puts nearly all twins\n     in other batches. Logits before the cut must match, which catches forward() looking ahead or across rows.\n  5. Seeds are drawn fresh unless given, and written to the log, so anyone can rerun the exact runs.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport ast\nimport builtins\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nimport platform\nimport secrets\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nimport types\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nimport stats  # noqa: E402\n\nTRACK = {\n    \"version\": \"odometer-v3\",\n    \"train_budget\": 40_000_000_000,  # ticks for everything train() does; about 80 s on a 4-core VM, 25 s on an M4\n    \"eval_ticks_per_byte\": 50_000,  # forward() price cap per scored byte\n    \"param_cap\": 1 << 22,  # floats in the returned parameters, plus characters in their names\n    \"source_cap\": 64 * 1024,  # bytes of train.py\n    \"literal_cap\": 4096,  # bytes of literals, keyword names and function names in train.py\n    \"node_cap\": 8192,  # syntax nodes in train.py; a table spelled in variable names has no literals to count\n    \"python_lines\": 20_000_000,  # entry lines and jumps per process\n    \"eval_context\": 512,\n    \"eval_batch\": 16,\n    \"eval_windows\": 1024,  # windows of eval_context bytes per held-out split\n    \"twin_fraction\": 0.25,\n    \"twin_positions\": 32,\n    \"twin_tolerance\": 1e-4,  # max |log p| difference between twins, in nats; a leak this small gains 1.4e-4 bits per byte\n    \"item_cap\": 20_000,  # item() reads in train()\n    \"wall_limit_seconds\": 3600,  # only catches hangs; it never decides a score\n}\nSMOKE = {\"train_budget\": 2_000_000_000, \"eval_windows\": 32, \"wall_limit_seconds\": 300}\nRECORD_ALPHA = 0.01\nRECORD_MARGIN = 0.002  # bits per byte a new record must clear on top of the significance test\nLOW_VARIANCE_RATIO = 0.3  # seed SD below this fraction of the incumbent's gets flagged for a human look\nTHREAD_VARS = (\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", \"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\", \"MKL_NUM_THREADS\", \"VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS\", \"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- static rules\n\nALLOWED_IMPORTS = {\"odometer\", \"math\"}\nALLOWED_BUILTINS = {\n    \"abs\", \"all\", \"any\", \"bool\", \"dict\", \"divmod\", \"enumerate\", \"float\", \"int\", \"isinstance\", \"len\", \"list\", \"max\",\n    \"min\", \"pow\", \"print\", \"range\", \"reversed\", \"round\", \"set\", \"sorted\", \"str\", \"sum\", \"tuple\", \"zip\",\n    \"True\", \"False\", \"None\",\n}\n# math without its functions over sequences and big integers, which do unbounded numeric work in one counted line\nMATH_NAMES = {n for n in dir(math) if not n.startswith(\"_\")} - {\n    \"comb\", \"dist\", \"factorial\", \"fsum\", \"gcd\", \"hypot\", \"isqrt\", \"lcm\", \"perm\", \"prod\", \"sumprod\",\n}\nCONTAINER_ATTRS = {\n    \"append\", \"extend\", \"insert\", \"pop\", \"remove\", \"reverse\", \"sort\", \"index\", \"count\", \"clear\", \"copy\", \"items\", \"keys\",\n    \"values\", \"get\", \"setdefault\", \"update\", \"join\", \"split\", \"strip\", \"startswith\", \"endswith\",\n}\nBANNED_NODES = (\n    ast.ClassDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef, ast.AsyncFor, ast.AsyncWith, ast.Await, ast.Try, ast.TryStar, ast.Match,\n    ast.Global, ast.Nonlocal, ast.Delete, ast.TypeAlias,\n)\n\n\ndef allowed_attrs():\n    import odometer as od\n\n    engine = {n for n in dir(od) if not n.startswith(\"_\")} - {\"Tensor\"}\n    tensor = {n for n in dir(od.Tensor) if not n.startswith(\"_\")}\n    return engine, engine | tensor | {\"batch\", \"num_bytes\"} | MATH_NAMES | CONTAINER_ATTRS\n\n\ndef is_constant_expr(node):\n    return all(isinstance(n, (ast.Constant, ast.Tuple, ast.UnaryOp, ast.BinOp, ast.Name, ast.Load, ast.operator, ast.unaryop))\n               for n in ast.walk(node))\n\n\ndef literal_bytes(tree):\n    \"\"\"Everything in the source an entry can read back as data. dict(name=1) and str(function) turn names into strings.\"\"\"\n    docstrings = {id(n.body[0].value) for n in ast.walk(tree)\n                  if isinstance(n, (ast.Module, ast.FunctionDef)) and n.body and isinstance(n.body[0], ast.Expr)\n                  and isinstance(n.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(n.body[0].value.value, str)}\n\n    def size(v):\n        if isinstance(v, str):\n            return len(v.encode(\"utf-8\", \"surrogatepass\"))\n        return len(v) if isinstance(v, bytes) else max(8, v.bit_length() // 8) if isinstance(v, int) else 8\n\n    total = 0\n    for n in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(n, ast.Constant) and id(n) not in docstrings:\n            total += size(n.value)\n        elif isinstance(n, ast.keyword) and n.arg:\n            total += size(n.arg)\n        elif isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef):\n            total += size(n.name)\n    return total\n\n\ndef static_problems(src, track=TRACK):\n    if len(src.encode()) > track[\"source_cap\"]:\n        return [f\"source is over {track['source_cap']} bytes\"]\n    try:\n        tree = ast.parse(src)\n    except (SyntaxError, MemoryError, RecursionError) as e:\n        return [f\"syntax error: {e}\"]\n    engine, attrs = allowed_attrs()\n    forbidden = set(dir(builtins)) - ALLOWED_BUILTINS\n    nodes = list(ast.walk(tree))\n    clears_grad = {id(t) for n in nodes if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and isinstance(n.value, ast.Constant) and n.value.value is None\n                   for t in n.targets if isinstance(t, ast.Attribute) and t.attr == \"grad\"}\n    problems = []\n    for node in nodes:\n        line = getattr(node, \"lineno\", 0)\n        if isinstance(node, BANNED_NODES):\n            problems.append(f\"line {line}: {type(node).__name__} is not allowed\")\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.Import):\n            problems += [f\"line {line}: import {a.name}\" for a in node.names if a.name not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS]\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom):\n            if node.level or node.module not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS:\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: from {'.' * node.level}{node.module or ''} import\")\n            else:\n                names = engine if node.module == \"odometer\" else MATH_NAMES\n                problems += [f\"line {line}: from {node.module} import {a.name}\" for a in node.names if a.name not in names]\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.alias):\n            if node.asname and node.asname.startswith(\"_\"):  # import math as __builtins__ swaps the builtins table\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.asname} starts with an underscore\")\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.Attribute):\n            if node.attr not in attrs:\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: .{node.attr} is not on the allowed list\")\n            if not isinstance(node.ctx, ast.Load) and id(node) not in clears_grad:\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: assigning to .{node.attr}\")\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.Name):\n            if node.id.startswith(\"_\") and node.id != \"_\":\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.id} starts with an underscore\")\n            elif node.id in forbidden:\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: builtin {node.id} is not on the allowed list\")\n        elif isinstance(node, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.Lambda)):\n            if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef):\n                if node.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: {node.name} starts with an underscore\")\n                if node.decorator_list:  # a decorator is a call at module level, so it could build state that persists\n                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: decorators are not allowed\")\n                if node.returns and not is_constant_expr(node.returns):\n                    problems.append(f\"line {line}: an annotation must be a constant\")\n            if not all(is_constant_expr(d) for d in [*node.args.defaults, *node.args.kw_defaults] if d is not None):\n                problems.append(f\"line {line}: a default argument must be a constant\")\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.arg) and node.annotation and not is_constant_expr(node.annotation):\n            problems.append(f\"line {line}: an annotation must be a constant\")  # annotations run once, at def time\n    for node in tree.body:\n        fine = isinstance(node, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom, ast.FunctionDef))\n        fine |= isinstance(node, ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.value, ast.Constant)\n        fine |= (isinstance(node, ast.Assign) and all(isinstance(t, ast.Name) for t in node.targets) and is_constant_expr(node.value))\n        if not fine:\n            problems.append(f\"line {node.lineno}: module level allows only imports, defs and constants\")\n    if literal_bytes(tree) > track[\"literal_cap\"]:\n        problems.append(f\"literals total {literal_bytes(tree)} bytes, over the cap of {track['literal_cap']}\")\n    if len(nodes) > track[\"node_cap\"]:\n        problems.append(f\"source has {len(nodes)} syntax nodes, over the cap of {track['node_cap']}\")\n    top = {n.name for n in tree.body if isinstance(n, ast.FunctionDef)}\n    problems += [f\"no top-level {f}()\" for f in (\"train\", \"forward\") if f not in top]\n    return problems\n\n\ndef load_entry(path, track):\n    \"\"\"Execute the entry with a builtins table that has no way out of the engine.\"\"\"\n    src = pathlib.Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    problems = static_problems(src, track)\n    if problems:\n        raise SystemExit(\"static rules failed:\\n  \" + \"\\n  \".join(problems))\n\n    def guarded_import(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0):\n        if level or name not in ALLOWED_IMPORTS:\n            raise ImportError(f\"import of {name} is not allowed\")\n        return builtins.__import__(name, globals, locals, fromlist, level)\n\n    safe = {k: getattr(builtins, k) for k in ALLOWED_BUILTINS}\n    safe[\"__import__\"] = guarded_import\n    module = types.ModuleType(\"entry\")\n    module.__dict__[\"__builtins__\"] = safe\n    exec(compile(src, str(path), \"exec\"), module.__dict__)\n    return module\n\n\ndef peak_rss_mb():\n    import resource\n\n    kb = resource.getrusage(resource.RUSAGE_SELF).ru_maxrss\n    return kb / 1024 ** (2 if sys.platform == \"darwin\" else 1)\n\n\ndef count_python_work(entry, cap, violation):\n    \"\"\"Deterministic fence on Python outside the engine: every line and jump of the entry costs one count.\"\"\"\n    mon, events = sys.monitoring, sys.monitoring.events\n    seen = [0]\n\n    def on_event(code, *rest):\n        if code.co_filename != entry:\n            return mon.DISABLE\n        seen[0] += 1\n        if seen[0] > cap:\n            raise violation(f\"more than {cap} Python lines and jumps in the entry\")\n\n    mon.use_tool_id(mon.PROFILER_ID, \"odometer\")\n    mon.register_callback(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.LINE, on_event)\n    mon.register_callback(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.JUMP, on_event)\n    mon.set_events(mon.PROFILER_ID, events.LINE | events.JUMP)\n    return seen\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the two child processes\n\n\ndef child_train(entry, seed, out):\n    import numpy as np\n\n    import odometer as od\n    from odometer import _data, _engine\n\n    out = pathlib.Path(out)\n    track = json.loads((out / \"track.json\").read_text())\n    _engine._M.reset(track[\"train_budget\"], seed, item_cap=track[\"item_cap\"])\n    data = _data.TrainData()\n    lines = count_python_work(entry, track[\"python_lines\"], od.RuleViolation)\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    status, params = \"ok\", None\n    try:\n        params = load_entry(entry, track).train(data)\n    except od.BudgetExhausted as e:\n        status = f\"void: BudgetExhausted escaped train() ({e})\"\n    except od.RuleViolation as e:\n        status = f\"void: rule violation: {e}\"\n    seconds = time.perf_counter() - t0\n    sys.monitoring.set_events(sys.monitoring.PROFILER_ID, 0)\n    if status == \"ok\":\n        if not isinstance(params, dict) or not all(isinstance(k, str) and type(v) is od.Tensor for k, v in params.items()):\n            status = \"void: train() must return a dict of name -> Tensor\"\n        elif any(v.is_int for v in params.values()):\n            status = \"void: parameters must be float tensors\"\n        elif sum(v.size + len(k) for k, v in params.items()) > track[\"param_cap\"]:\n            status = f\"void: more than {track['param_cap']} parameters, with one more per character of their names\"\n        else:\n            np.savez(out / \"params.npz\", **{f\"p{i}\": v._d for i, v in enumerate(params.values())})\n            (out / \"names.json\").write_text(json.dumps(list(params)))\n    report = {\"status\": status, \"train_ticks\": _engine._M.used, \"train_seconds\": seconds, \"item_reads\": _engine._M.items,\n              \"train_python_lines\": lines[0], \"peak_rss_mb\": peak_rss_mb(), \"params\": sum(v.size for v in params.values()) if status == \"ok\" else None}\n    (out / \"train.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report))\n\n\ndef child_eval(entry, seed, split, out):\n    import numpy as np\n\n    import odometer as od\n    from odometer import _data, _engine\n\n    out = pathlib.Path(out)\n    track = json.loads((out / \"track.json\").read_text())\n    C, B = track[\"eval_context\"], track[\"eval_batch\"]\n    windows = _data.heldout_windows(split, C, track[\"eval_windows\"])\n    n = len(windows)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng([seed, 2])\n    twins = np.sort(rng.choice(n, int(n * track[\"twin_fraction\"]), replace=False))\n    cuts = rng.integers(1, C, size=twins.size)\n    donors = windows[rng.integers(0, n, size=twins.size)]\n    rows = np.concatenate([windows[:, :C], windows[twins, :C]])\n    probe = []\n    for j, (cut, donor) in enumerate(zip(cuts, donors)):\n        rows[n + j, cut:] = donor[cut:C]\n        last = np.arange(max(0, cut - 8), cut)  # a look-ahead leak shows first just before the cut\n        probe.append(np.union1d(last, rng.choice(cut, min(cut, track[\"twin_positions\"]), replace=False)))\n    probe_rows = {int(r): j for j, r in enumerate(twins)} | {n + j: j for j in range(twins.size)}\n    order = rng.permutation(len(rows))\n\n    scored_bytes = len(rows) * C\n    _engine._M.reset(track[\"eval_ticks_per_byte\"] * scored_bytes, seed, mode=\"eval\")\n    lines = count_python_work(entry, track[\"python_lines\"], od.RuleViolation)\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    status = \"ok\"\n    nll = np.zeros(n)\n    seen = {}\n    try:\n        module = load_entry(entry, track)\n        names = json.loads((out / \"names.json\").read_text())\n        stored = np.load(out / \"params.npz\")\n        arrays = {name: stored[f\"p{i}\"] for i, name in enumerate(names)}\n        for a in arrays.values():\n            a.setflags(write=False)\n        for start in range(0, len(rows), B):\n            idx = order[start : start + B]\n            logits = module.forward({k: od.Tensor(a) for k, a in arrays.items()}, od.Tensor(rows[idx].astype(np.int32)))\n            if type(logits) is not od.Tensor or logits.is_int or logits.shape != (len(idx), C, od.VOCAB):\n                raise od.RuleViolation(f\"forward() must return float logits of shape (batch, {C}, {od.VOCAB})\")\n            z = logits._d.astype(np.float64)\n            if not np.isfinite(z).all():\n                raise od.RuleViolation(\"forward() returned non-finite logits\")\n            lp = z - z.max(-1, keepdims=True)\n            lp -= np.log(np.exp(lp).sum(-1, keepdims=True))\n            for b, r in enumerate(idx):\n                if r < n:\n                    nll[r] = -lp[b, np.arange(C), windows[r, 1:]].sum()\n                if int(r) in probe_rows:\n                    j = probe_rows[int(r)]\n                    seen.setdefault(j, []).append(lp[b, probe[j]])\n    except od.BudgetExhausted:\n        status = f\"void: forward() cost more than {track['eval_ticks_per_byte']:,} ticks per byte\"\n    except od.RuleViolation as e:\n        status = f\"void: rule violation: {e}\"\n    sys.monitoring.set_events(sys.monitoring.PROFILER_ID, 0)\n    twin_diff = max((float(np.abs(a - b).max()) for a, b in seen.values()), default=0.0) if status == \"ok\" else None\n    if status == \"ok\" and twin_diff > track[\"twin_tolerance\"]:\n        status = f\"void: twin check failed (logits before the cut moved by {twin_diff:.2e} nats)\"\n    report = {\"status\": status, \"split\": split, \"bpb\": float(nll.sum() / (n * C) / np.log(2)) if status == \"ok\" else None,\n              \"eval_ticks_per_byte\": _engine._M.used / scored_bytes, \"twin_max_diff\": twin_diff,\n              \"eval_python_lines\": lines[0], \"eval_seconds\": time.perf_counter() - t0}\n    (out / \"eval.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report))\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the parent\n\n\ndef run_seed(entry, seed, split, track, keep):\n    env = {\"PATH\": os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"\"), **{v: \"1\" for v in THREAD_VARS}}\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        (pathlib.Path(tmp) / \"track.json\").write_text(json.dumps(track))\n        result = {\"seed\": seed}\n        for stage, extra in ((\"train\", []), (\"eval\", [split])):\n            cmd = [sys.executable, \"-I\", str(ROOT / \"verify.py\"), f\"--child-{stage}\", str(entry), str(seed), *extra, tmp]\n            log = keep / f\"seed-{seed}-{stage}.log\"\n            try:\n                with open(log, \"wb\") as sink:\n                    subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=tmp, env=env, stdout=sink, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=track[\"wall_limit_seconds\"])\n            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n                result[\"status\"] = f\"void: {stage} process passed the wall limit\"\n                return result\n            path = pathlib.Path(tmp) / f\"{stage}.json\"\n            if not path.exists():\n                result[\"status\"] = f\"void: {stage} process crashed (see {log.name})\"\n                return result\n            result |= json.loads(path.read_text())\n            if result[\"status\"] != \"ok\":\n                return result\n        return result\n\n\ndef machine():\n    import numpy as np\n\n    blas = np.show_config(mode=\"dicts\")[\"Build Dependencies\"][\"blas\"]\n    return {\"platform\": platform.platform(), \"machine\": platform.machine(), \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n            \"numpy\": np.__version__, \"blas\": f\"{blas.get('name')} {blas.get('version')}\", \"cpus\": os.cpu_count()}\n\n\ndef code_hash():\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    for p in [ROOT / \"verify.py\", *sorted((ROOT / \"odometer\").glob(\"*.py\"))]:\n        h.update(p.read_bytes())\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef run_batch(entry, seeds, split, track, logs, jobs, label=\"\"):\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(jobs) as pool:\n        results = []\n        for r in pool.map(lambda s: run_seed(entry, s, split, track, logs), seeds):\n            results.append(r)\n            if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\":\n                print(f\"  seed {r['seed']:>10}  {split} bpb {r['bpb']:.4f}  train {r['train_ticks']:.3e} ticks  \"\n                      f\"{r['train_seconds']:6.1f} s  eval {r['eval_ticks_per_byte']:,.0f} ticks/byte  \"\n                      f\"twins {r['twin_max_diff']:.1e}{label}\", flush=True)\n            else:\n                print(f\"  seed {r['seed']:>10}  {r['status']}{label}\", flush=True)\n    return results\n\n\ndef fresh_seeds(n):\n    return [secrets.randbits(31) for _ in range(n)]\n\n\ndef judge(bpbs, record_bpbs):\n    \"\"\"Does this batch beat the record by more than the margin? Welch, one-sided, on the verifier's own seeds.\"\"\"\n    w = stats.welch(bpbs, [b - RECORD_MARGIN for b in record_bpbs])\n    plain = stats.welch(bpbs, record_bpbs)\n    return {\"gain\": -plain[\"diff\"], \"ci95\": plain[\"ci95\"], \"df\": w[\"df\"], \"p_beyond_margin\": w[\"p_one_sided\"],\n            \"passes\": w[\"p_one_sided\"] < RECORD_ALPHA}\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    ap.add_argument(\"entry\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seeds\", default=\"8\", help=\"a count of fresh seeds, or a comma list to rerun exact seeds ('11,' is seed 11)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--split\", default=\"test\", choices=(\"dev\", \"test\"))\n    ap.add_argument(\"--jobs\", type=int, default=0, help=\"seeds in parallel (default: min(seeds, cpus))\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--against\", help=\"a record log; tests whether this entry beats it, then confirms on new seeds\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--smoke\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"a tiny budget and a few windows; the number is not a score\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", help=\"where to write the log (default runs/<entry>-<time>.json)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    track = {**TRACK, **SMOKE} if args.smoke else TRACK\n    entry = pathlib.Path(args.entry).resolve()\n    src = entry.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    problems = static_problems(src, track)\n    if problems:\n        print(\"static rules failed:\\n  \" + \"\\n  \".join(problems))\n        sys.exit(2)\n    seeds = [int(s) for s in args.seeds.split(\",\") if s] if \",\" in args.seeds else fresh_seeds(int(args.seeds))\n    name = entry.parent.name if entry.name == \"train.py\" else entry.stem\n    stamp = time.strftime(\"%Y%m%d-%H%M%S\")\n    out = pathlib.Path(args.out) if args.out else ROOT / \"runs\" / f\"{name}-{stamp}.json\"\n    logs = out.with_suffix(\"\")\n    logs.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    jobs = args.jobs or max(1, min(len(seeds), os.cpu_count() or 1))\n    print(f\"{name}: {len(seeds)} seeds on {args.split}, {jobs} at a time, budget {track['train_budget']:.1e} ticks\"\n          + (\" (smoke run: not a score)\" if args.smoke else \"\"), flush=True)\n\n    t0 = time.time()\n    results = run_batch(entry, seeds, args.split, track, logs, jobs)\n    ok = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in results if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\"]\n    log = {\"entry\": str(entry.relative_to(ROOT)) if entry.is_relative_to(ROOT) else entry.name,\n           \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(src.encode()).hexdigest(), \"code_sha256\": code_hash(), \"track\": track,\n           \"split\": args.split, \"smoke\": args.smoke, \"machine\": machine(), \"started\": stamp, \"seeds\": results}\n    if len(ok) == len(results) and len(ok) >= 2:\n        m, half = stats.ci95(ok)\n        log[\"summary\"] = {\"mean_bpb\": m, \"ci95\": half, \"sd\": stats.mean_sd(ok)[1], \"n\": len(ok)}\n        print(f\"  mean {m:.4f} +- {half:.4f} bpb (95% CI, n={len(ok)}, sd {log['summary']['sd']:.4f})\")\n    elif len(ok) != len(results):\n        print(\"  void: at least one seed failed, so the entry has no score\")\n    elif ok:\n        print(f\"  {ok[0]:.4f} bpb on one seed (use at least 2 for an interval)\")\n\n    if args.against and \"summary\" in log:\n        inc = json.loads(pathlib.Path(args.against).read_text())\n        if inc[\"split\"] != args.split:\n            raise SystemExit(\"the record was scored on a different split\")\n        incumbent = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in inc.get(\"confirmation\", inc[\"seeds\"])]\n        stage1 = judge(ok, incumbent)\n        verdict = {\"against\": args.against, \"margin\": RECORD_MARGIN, \"alpha\": RECORD_ALPHA, \"stage1\": stage1, \"record\": False}\n        print(f\"  gain over the record: {stage1['gain']:+.4f} +- {stage1['ci95']:.4f} bpb, p = {stage1['p_beyond_margin']:.2g} \"\n              f\"(beyond a margin of {RECORD_MARGIN})\")\n        if stats.mean_sd(ok)[1] < LOW_VARIANCE_RATIO * stats.mean_sd(incumbent)[1]:\n            verdict[\"flag\"] = \"seed SD is far below the incumbent's; read the entry for a fixed init or data order\"\n            print(f\"  flag: {verdict['flag']}\")\n        if stage1[\"passes\"]:\n            print(\"  passed; confirming on new seeds\", flush=True)\n            second = run_batch(entry, fresh_seeds(len(seeds)), args.split, track, logs, jobs, label=\"  (confirmation)\")\n            log[\"confirmation\"] = second\n            good = [r[\"bpb\"] for r in second if r[\"status\"] == \"ok\"]\n  